%% ROC module/port/adapter seams (engineer-owned change-impact model).
%% *** RENDERABILITY, SECOND FAULT (DEF-ROC-042, 2026-08-24) - THIS FILE BROKE AGAIN. ***
%% Delta 019 quoted every label and the file rendered; it then broke again within days and
%% nothing noticed, because `scripts/check-docs.mjs` still never opened a standalone .mmd file.
%% The fault was at line ~224 (`soakSweep`): a LITERAL double-quote inside an already
%% double-quoted label - tickets [<quote>ROC-1<quote>,<quote>ROC-2<quote>]. The inner quote
%% CLOSES the label, so mermaid reported `Parse error on line 80 ... Expecting SQE, got STR`,
%% a message pointing NOWHERE NEAR the edit. Worse, at mermaids DEFAULT maxTextSize that parse
%% error was entirely MASKED: mmdc EXITED 0 and wrote a 9,460-byte "Maximum text size in
%% diagram exceeded" ERROR IMAGE, so no exit-code gate could ever have seen it.
%% CONVENTION EXTENDED: a quote INSIDE a label is written #quot; (mermaid renders it as a real ").
%% THIS IS NOW GATED, so it should not need hand-finding a third time:
%%   make check-docs      - delegates to scripts/check-mmd.mjs (lint + REAL render, and the
%%                          verdict is taken from the rendered OUTPUT, never mmdc exit status)
%%   node scripts/check-mmd.mjs --lint-only   - instant; also runs in the app unit suite as
%%                          src/app/tests/unit/def042-mmd-renderability.test.ts
%% *** RENDERABILITY (delta 019, 2026-08-18) — THIS FILE DID NOT RENDER AT ALL BEFORE THIS DELTA. ***
%% Two independent faults, both pre-existing: (1) it exceeds mermaid's default `maxTextSize`, so
%% mmdc exits 0 while writing a ~9KB "Maximum text size in diagram exceeded" ERROR image — a zero
%% exit code is NOT evidence of a render; (2) with the limit raised it then failed with a PARSE
%% ERROR on a bare `(` inside a node label. Nothing caught either: `scripts/check-docs.mjs` renders
%% only ```mermaid FENCED blocks in .md and is BLIND to the standalone *.mmd files (DEF-ROC-042's
%% class, still open). Fixed by QUOTING every node and edge label.
%% CONVENTION FROM NOW ON: every node label and every edge label in this file is DOUBLE-QUOTED.
%% VERIFY with: printf '{"maxTextSize":900000,"maxEdges":2000}' > /tmp/mmdc.json &&
%%   npx @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i architecture/dependencies/class-deps.mmd -o /tmp/cd.svg \
%%   --configFile /tmp/mmdc.json    (expect a MULTI-HUNDRED-KB svg, not ~9KB)
%% Hexagonal: adapters + functions depend on domain-defined PORTS; domain
%% depends on nothing concrete. Edges are ACTUAL runtime routing, not intended.
%% classDef s002changed marks nodes added/redirected by UC-ROC-002 (NORMALISE +
%% Table Storage decision log); classDef s003changed marks nodes changed by
%% UC-ROC-003 (pattern-based site-derivation + NOT-HANDLED outcome) — both are
%% the tester's test-plan input; cleared to :::stable at slice delivery.
%% classDef s004changed marks nodes added/redirected by UC-ROC-004 (rules engine +
%% seeded UYD rule set; pipeline rule step redirected from the hardcoded HDCERR1
%% rule to the rules-engine decision; decisionRecord now carries firing-rule /
%% template provenance) — tester test-plan input; cleared to :::stable at delivery.
%% UC-ROC-001's nodes are now :::stable (that use-case is done).
%% @covers/node-id RECONCILIATION (OI-COVERS-NODEID, tester-added 2026-07-23):
