%% config- prefixed vocabulary (e.g. `domain-decisionRecord`) rather than this
%% diagram's terse bare node ids (e.g. `decisionRecord`). Without an alias every
%% changed prefixed-tag node false-reports UNCOVERED to impacted-tests even when a
%% real covering spec exists (found validating UC-ROC-048: consumer/decisionRecord
%% both showed uncovered despite consumerDeBounce.test.ts + deBounceDecision.test.ts
%% covering them). These aliases are the reconciliation — keep in sync as new
%% prefixed tags are added.
