flowchart TD
    %% --- ports (domain-defined interfaces) ---
    telPort("[TelemetrySourcePort]")
    logProdPort("[LogProducerPort]")
    logConsPort("[LogConsumerPort]")
    jiraPort("[JiraPort<br/>createAlert + createNewTypeTicket second KIND]")
    alertStatePort("[AlertStatePort<br/>append + queryByIdentity + claimFirstUnrecognisedType + UC-049 listExpiredHolds now point-in-time query + claimSoakExpiry insert-if-not-exists; DEF-ROC-049 ADDS releaseSoakExpiryClaim + releaseFirstUnrecognisedTypeClaim - REQUIRED not optional (v124) because a store that can claim but not un-claim silently reinstates the burnt claim: the claim IS the assertion 'a ticket may exist for this hold with no raised record', and a REFUSED create falsifies it; NO change feed]")
    decisionLogQueryPort("[DecisionLogQueryPort<br/>list outcome/site/since; read-only; cross-alert review; NO change feed]")
    ruleConfigStorePort("[RuleConfigStorePort<br/>UC-056 config authoring: saveDraft/getDraft/listDrafts/discardDraft append-only DRAFT CRUD + listVersions published-fold read; UC-057 putTestAttestation/readTestAttestation; UC-058 appendVersion immutable version row per-ruleId monotonic version idempotent-on-attestation-hash CC-3; UC-059 allocateRuleId globally-unique claim-by-insert id mint CC-7/9 + RuleIdAllocationExhaustedError; NO change feed; DynamoDB adapter satisfiable]")
    sitePatternStorePort("[SitePatternStorePort<br/>UC-064 NEW port site-pattern authoring DRAFT half: saveDraft/getDraft/listDrafts/discardDraft over SitePatternDraft iata+pattern + savedBy; idempotent-on-content created:false AC-064-2; NOT RuleConfigStorePort iata-keyed not rule-shaped; NO change feed; DynamoDB adapter satisfiable; listVersions/appendVersion + attestation markers are LATER UCs]")
    siteTemplateLinkStorePort("[SiteTemplateLinkStorePort<br/>UC-068 site to template LINK registry: listLinkVersions raw persisted link rows Query/Get; __sitetemplatelink__ partition of SitePatternConfig NOT a field on SitePattern patternless BHX NOT a new table same custody+grant; current link set = FOLD over SEEDED_SITE_TEMPLATE_LINKS baseline; UC-071 delta015 gains its FIRST WRITE appendLink - reads-then-writes fold-current + conditional INSERT idempotent-on-store-latest-row CC-U3, tombstone omits templateId col; §30 pin WIDENED Query/Get/Insert still existing grant NO widening; NO change feed]")
    soakTriggerPort("[SoakTriggerPort<br/>UC-049 time-driven sweep trigger; start pass -> stop; LOCAL setInterval / PROD Azure Timer adapter swap]")
    secretPort("[SecretPort]")

    %% --- adapters (one external concept each) ---
    sbSource["ServiceBusTelemetrySource<br/>TWO config-selected auth shapes UC-019: LOCAL connectionString/SAS emulator vs DEV/PROD fullyQualifiedNamespace+TokenCredential DefaultAzureCredential -> Function user-assigned MI Service Bus Data Receiver against disableLocalAuth namespace; ServiceBusClient constructor INJECTED so contract-tested NO live SB; fail-fast on incomplete shape; peek-lock complete/abandon unchanged"]
    ehProducer["EventHubsLogProducer<br/>TWO config-selected auth shapes UC-020: LOCAL connectionString/SAS emulator vs DEV/PROD fullyQualifiedNamespace+eventHubName+TokenCredential DefaultAzureCredential -> forwarder Function user-assigned MI Event Hubs Data Sender against disableLocalAuth namespace; EventHubProducerClient constructor INJECTED so contract-tested NO live EH; fail-fast on incomplete shape; batch/send unchanged"]
    ehConsumer["EventHubsLogConsumer<br/>messageId = source id, not EH sequence; TWO config-selected auth shapes UC-020: LOCAL connectionString/SAS vs DEV/PROD fqns+eventHubName+TokenCredential -> consumer Function user-assigned MI Event Hubs Data Receiver + consumer-group; EventHubConsumerClient constructor + Blob checkpoint-store factory INJECTED so contract-tested NO live EH/Blob; fail-fast on incomplete shape; earliest-start/checkpoint-after-onEvent semantics unchanged; DEF-031 receive errors CLASSIFIED not swallowed: a stolen partition ReceiverDisconnectedError/amqp:link:stolen is a NAMED PartitionStolenError under exclusive ownership (stop rejects + competingConsumerDetected for fail-fast, category concurrent-consumer) vs benign warn-level partition-rebalance under shared ownership DEV/PROD default"]
    fakeJira["FakeJiraAdapter<br/>createdAlerts + newTypeTickets logs"]
    jiraApi["JiraApiAdapter<br/>OAuth2 client-creds token mint+cache+refresh; shared postIssue for createAlert + createNewTypeTicket; 4xx internal / 5xx external; NOT wired into LOCAL e2e"]
    unavailableJira["UnavailableJiraAdapter<br/>DEF-ROC-021 NEW the DEGRADED JiraPort: every method REFUSES with JiraEgressUnavailableError + one categorised jira.egress.unavailable line naming the op + a distinguishable reason CODE disabled-by-flag/tenant-mismatch/vault-not-configured/vault-uri-invalid/vault-access-denied/secret-not-found/secret-empty/credential-unresolvable/unknown; category derived per the failure taxonomy - credential-unresolvable is external-availability the rest are internal-configuration our own misconfiguration; DELIBERATELY NOT FakeJiraAdapter - the fake RETURNS a key so the consumer would append raised+jiraKey for a ticket that does not exist which IS DEF-ROC-012; payload params declared PARAMETER-LESS so nothing sent can be read/logged/retained; classifyJiraEgressFailure maps a construction failure to the reason CODE off our own value-free adapter messages + the @azure/identity error names, unmatched -> unknown never a guess"]
    tableStore["TableStorageAlertStore<br/>@azure/data-tables; insert-if-not-exists; ticks RowKey; __unrecognised__ dedup marker; TWO config-selected auth shapes UC-025: LOCAL connectionString/Azurite via fromConnectionString vs DEV/PROD tableEndpoint+TokenCredential DefaultAzureCredential -> consumer Function user-assigned MI Storage Table Data Contributor against shared_access_key_enabled=false account; TableClient factory INJECTED so contract-tested NO live Table Storage; fail-fast on incomplete shape/missing endpoint; UC-049 listExpiredHolds ($filter outcome eq held-until + pure filterExpiredHolds instant-compare) + claimSoakExpiry (__soak_expiry__ marker, createEntity only — no new op type); DEF-ROC-049 releaseSoakExpiryClaim = deleteEntity on that SAME marker key, 404-idempotent, and it needs a WIDER client capability (ClaimReleasingTableClientLike) that is deliberately NOT added to the shared TableClientLike - the append-only config stores reuse that type and their §30 pin is createEntity+listEntities ONLY, so widening it would hand a delete to every store forbidden to make one. The append-only decision log is still never deleted from: what is released is a CLAIM in a reserved marker partition, not a record"]
    tableStoreQuery["TableStorageDecisionLogQuery<br/>@azure/data-tables; READ-ONLY listEntities; server-side $filter narrows ONLY on the caller outcome/site, pure projectDecisionRows authoritative; newest-first. DEF-ROC-098: what is projected is decided by a POSITIVE SHAPE PREDICATE isDecisionRow - the columns toRecord and the ordering dereference - NOT by an enumerated list of reserved partition names. The old blacklist named three of the four reserved partitions of the SHARED AlertDecisions table and UC-101 added the fourth (__simpublish__), so the UNFILTERED GET /api/decisions threw and answered 503 on the deployed host while ?outcome=raised answered 200. A reserved partition nobody has written yet is now excluded by construction; a DECISION-shaped row in a reserved partition (the DEF-ROC-030 quarantine) stays visible; a damaged row in a real identity partition is dropped from the payload and reported as decision-log-poison-row rather than taking the whole surface down"]
    ruleConfigStore["TableStorageRuleConfigStore<br/>UC-056 @azure/data-tables NEW dedicated RuleConfig table; SAME two auth shapes as tableStore LOCAL connectionString/Azurite vs DEV/PROD endpoint+TokenCredential MI Storage Table Data Contributor; APPEND-ONLY createEntity+listEntities ONLY §30 pin no update/merge/delete; drafts partition draft|scope|id fold-latest + discard tombstone; published partition scope|id fold-tolerant skip-poison; UC-058 appendVersion INSERT-only immutable version rows ticks+seq tie-break CC-1 fold=max-ticks CC-4/6; UC-059 allocateRuleId claim-by-insert on __ruleidalloc__ high-water partition floor=max seeded/published static id bounded recompute-retry <=5 still createEntity+listEntities ONLY; TableClient factory INJECTED contract-tested NO live Table Storage"]
    sitePatternStore["TableStorageSitePatternStore<br/>UC-064 @azure/data-tables NEW dedicated SitePatternConfig table; SAME two auth shapes as tableStore LOCAL connectionString/Azurite vs DEV/PROD endpoint+TokenCredential MI Storage Table Data Contributor; APPEND-ONLY createEntity+listEntities ONLY §30 pin no update/merge/delete; DRAFT half only __sitedraft__ partition RowKey iata+savedTicks+monotonic-seq fold-latest-per-iata + discard tombstone; TableClient factory INJECTED contract-tested NO live Table Storage"]
    siteTemplateLinkStore["TableStorageSiteTemplateLinkStore<br/>UC-068 @azure/data-tables adapter over __sitetemplatelink__ PARTITION of the EXISTING SitePatternConfig table NOT a new table; SAME auth shapes+selection as sitePatternStore reuses existing Storage Table Data Contributor grant NO widening; listLinkVersions = createTable+listEntities; UC-071 delta015 appendLink INSERT-only reads-then-writes fold-current + createEntity RowKey iata+linkedTicksD19+seq tombstone omits templateId col, §30 pin WIDENED createTable+listEntities+createEntity ONLY no update/merge/delete; TableClient factory INJECTED contract-tested NO live Table Storage"]
    envSecret["EnvSecretAdapter"]
    jsonSecret["JsonFileSecretAdapter<br/>LOCAL-only; reads work/ROC/secrets/jira.json at resolve time; maps ROC_JIRA_CLIENT_ID/SECRET -> client_id/client_secret; base_url/cloud_id via getConfig NOT getSecret; fail-fast, value-free errors/logs; NOT wired into any entrypoint (UC-016)"]
    kvSecret["KeyVaultSecretAdapter<br/>DEV/PROD; @azure/identity DefaultAzureCredential -> Function user-assigned managed identity + @azure/keyvault-secrets SecretClient; reads KEY_VAULT_URI; maps ROC_JIRA_CLIENT_ID/SECRET -> roc-jira-client-id/-secret KV names; fail-fast value-free on unreachable/missing/AccessDenied/value-less; id-only logs never the value; SecretClient INJECTED so contract-tested with NO live Azure UC-018"]
    easyAuthPrincipal["adapters/auth/easyAuthPrincipal<br/>UC-081 NEW CLOUD-HOST identity seam REQ-005 AC-2/3/4: derivePrincipal reads ONE header the platform-injected Easy Auth token-store x-ms-client-principal base64 JSON claims -> role admin UNIFORMLY for every authenticated principal no claim differentiates it J28 stays deferred + user from UPN-style claims first preferred_username/upn then name_typ then display names so append-only publishedBy attribution is unambiguous never local-dev; FAILS CLOSED absent/empty/malformed/claim-less -> authenticated:false + reason NO default-to-admin NO placeholder; NEVER reads x-roc-role/x-roc-user on any code path - the PARALLEL SEPARATE derivation to local/read-api's caller-trusted headers not a guard bolted onto it AC-081-3/4 HARD pinned adversarially + by a header-lookup recorder + source pins; NO EDGES YET deliberately unwired - DEF-ROC-009 imports it when it registers cloud admin routes and Easy Auth handoff Ask D is enabled; TRUST ANCHOR is the platform stripping client-supplied copies of the header under require-authentication - this module cannot verify that itself"]

    %% --- UC-ROC-009 read boundary + dashboard SPA (LOCAL) ---
    readApi["local/read-api<br/>HTTP boundary: GET /api/decisions?outcome/site/since -> DecisionLogQueryPort.list filter -> JSON; POST /api/evaluate now STORE-BACKED via evaluateApi deps AC-058-5; UC-056 GET /api/rules + POST /api/rules/draft + /api/rules/draft/discard -> rulesApi; UC-058 POST /api/rules/publish -> publishApi; UC-059 POST /api/rules/new -> rulesApi.createRuleDraft + makeRulesDeps injects allocation floor from SEEDED_RULES; UC-062 GET /api/rules/history?site&ruleId -> rulesApi.getRuleHistory read-role-gated read-only; UC-063 POST /api/rules/restore {site,ruleId,version} -> rulesApi.restoreVersion admin-role write-path gate; ReadApiOverrides TEST-inject seam Azurite-free routes; x-roc-build header + /api/health buildSha principle 01; Node host of the port; Azure Function later, SPA unchanged"]
    jiraTicketUrl["src/domain/jiraTicketUrl<br/>DEF-ROC-116 NEW the ticket BROWSE url seam: resolveJiraBrowseBase(env) ONE setting ROC_JIRA_BROWSE_BASE_URL https-only bare-origin refuse-whole; jiraTicketUrl(base,KEY) anchored key regex; withJiraTicketUrl non-mutating additive; PURE no SDK; read PER REQUEST by BOTH decision-log roots so the browser never learns a Jira host"]
    readApiFilter["local/readApiFilter<br/>parseDecisionFilter: URLSearchParams -> DecisionLogFilter; empty param omits dimension; NO query logic"]
    sitesApi["src/api/sitesApi<br/>UC-064 site-pattern authoring write boundary seam transport-free: getSites -> baseline SEEDED_SITES published patterns + listDrafts + publishDisabled; saveSiteDraft ADMIN-GATE-FIRST 403 non-admin AC-064-5 then validateSiteDraft 400-never-persisted then store.saveDraft idempotent; discardSiteDraft admin-gated; savedBy attribution; role from x-roc-role header default admin LOCAL loopback; UC-087 getSites FAILS SAFE: the published-pattern list is read INDEPENDENTLY of the drafts so the DRAFT read is ORDERED SECOND and GUARDED - a refused SitePatternConfig draft read narrows to drafts:[] + in-band draftsUnavailable + a categorised external-availability line instead of discarding the ENTIRE response into read-api's flat 503 (pre-fix a single awaited listDrafts sank 90% of an answer that never needed it); notice ABSENT on a healthy read AC-087-2; the WRITE paths saveSiteDraft/discardSiteDraft/siteDraftTest/sitePublish are UNTOUCHED and still THROW - sitePublish's readTestAttestation read stays STRICT because a lenient read there would turn an unreachable store into a gate verdict; UC-088 MOVED local/sitesApi -> src/api/sitesApi (import paths only, behaviour byte-identical) for the same reason: tsconfig.functions.json builds the deployed zip from src and EXCLUDES local so getSites was not in the deployed bundle; getSites is now served by BOTH local/read-api and src/host/configReadHttp - ONE seam two composition roots; saveSiteDraft/discardSiteDraft/siteDraftTest/sitePublish stay LOCAL-ONLY; DEF-ROC-065 getSites AND siteDraftTest now READ THE FOLD: both took their published-site answer from the SEEDED_SITES baseline CONSTANT (getSites mapped deps.baseline into publishedPattern; siteDraftTest set currentSites = deps.baseline for its BEFORE column) while the live pipeline readThroughSitesFor and the Simulator evaluateApi resolved through loadEffectiveSitePatterns - so from UC-066 onwards this authoring screen could name a pattern the pipeline had stopped resolving on, and the regression/gap-closing-gain delta was measured against a catalogue not in force (measured: 10 real PPSM node names where the screen said UYD and the pipeline resolved NOT-HANDLED). NEW EDGE sitesApi --> loadEffectiveSitePatterns; deps.baseline survives ONLY as the loader FLOOR, so two readers of one fact become one reader plus a projection (EXP-047). The UC-087 fail-safe is PRESERVED but its MECHANISM moved: the site list no longer avoids the store, it relies on the loader degrading to the SAME SEEDED_SITES floor the pipeline degrades to, so even a refused read cannot make the screen disagree with the pipeline; JSON-portable to Azure Function"]
    evaluateApi["src/api/evaluateApi<br/>UC-033 evaluate boundary parity-rewired UC-058: parseEvaluateRequest validate author-event missing/unknown device+status -> 400; resolves site then folds the SHARED RuleConfig store via loadEffectiveCatalogue the SAME read the pipeline uses NO SEEDED_RULES import DEF-005 code-seam pin; evaluateRequest async -> evaluateWithTrace; NO eval logic; JSON-portable to Azure Function; UC-074 delta015 optional linkResolver: resolves the parent PER REQUEST via snapshotTemplateOf() replacing the frozen-seed seededSiteTemplateOf so a relink is reflected in the Simulator NO redeploy - the mirror-surface parity seam reads the SAME source the live pipeline does; UC-084 MOVED local/evaluateApi -> src/api/evaluateApi: the transport-free seam is now inside the FUNCTIONS BUILD ROOT (tsconfig.functions.json include:[src] rootDir:src excludes local/) so the DEPLOYED host can import it - the local read-api and the cloud host are TWO composition roots over ONE seam, never a second implementation; behaviour byte-identical (import paths only); DEF-ROC-017 the catalogue read now goes through loadEffectiveCatalogueForSiteResult so a refused RuleConfig read yields a USABLE 200 on the seeded baseline instead of a thrown 503 - and the 200 carries an explicit rulesDegraded notice degradedToBaseline+category:external-availability+message+detail so a support engineer can never mistake a seeded answer for a published one (UC-084 own-done 5 intent preserved; the DEF-ROC-013 benign-looking-failure lesson); the notice is ABSENT on the happy path so the body stays byte-identical to evaluateWithTrace AC-033-1"]
    evaluateHttp["src/host/evaluateHttp<br/>UC-084 the DEPLOYED host's HTTP adapter for /api/evaluate: EVALUATE_ROUTE data-shape POST+anonymous+route:evaluate; makeEvaluateHandler(getDeps) reads the body then calls the ONE shared evaluateRequest seam - NO evaluation logic and NO second parse; registerEvaluateRoute(app,getDeps) so the registration NAME/method/authLevel is assertable without the Functions runtime; failure taxonomy: non-JSON or parse failure = caller-data 400 with the EXISTING message, store-read failure = categorised external-availability 503 NEVER a false 200 (UC-084 own-done 5); DEF-ROC-017 landed the degrade-to-baseline inside the SHARED loader so the live pipeline gets it too - all three config reads now fail SAFE so this route answers 200-with-rulesDegraded for a refused RuleConfig read and the 503 covers only what the loaders do NOT own"]
    evaluateForHost["src/host/evaluateForHost<br/>UC-084 the CLOUD composition root for /api/evaluate - the deployed twin of read-api's makeEvaluateDeps, field for field: RuleConfig store + SEEDED_RULES baseline + STORE-BACKED link resolver read per request (UC-074, never the frozen seed) + SitePatternConfig store + SEEDED_SITES floor; reuses composition.ts's defaultRuleConfigStore/defaultSitePatternStore so the cloud Simulator and the live consumer share ONE store-auth decision (EXP-047); lazyEvaluateDeps memoises on FIRST REQUEST so host import touches no store and a cold start / health probe cannot be broken by table reachability; DEPLOYED AUTH SHAPE verified live 2026-07-31: the Function App sets TABLESTORAGE_ENDPOINT so BOTH stores select MANAGED IDENTITY - whose grant covers AlertDecisions ONLY today, so a CONFIGURED-site rule read is refused until platform Ask A widens it to storage-account scope; deliberately does NOT fall back to the account-key AzureWebJobsStorage that /api/decisions uses (routing config reads around the MI to dodge a pending grant is a security-posture change the architect owns)"]
    azureFunctionsHost["src/azure-functions<br/>UC-024 the deployed Function App's HTTP surface, registered at module import via app.http: health liveness+dependency reachability and decisions the decision-log read; UC-084 adds the THIRD route evaluate (anonymous, read-only, per REQ-ROC-005/CHK-ROC-011's explicit /api/evaluate gating carve-out). DELIBERATELY ABSENT: /api/rules* and /api/sites* - they carry admin WRITES (save draft, publish, restore, relink) and registering them on this public-internet hostname before the Easy Auth gate (platform Ask D) would put unauthenticated administrative writes on the internet; they stay 404 here on purpose (DEF-ROC-009), pinned by an EXACT route-registration assertion. UC-088 adds the fourth/fifth/sixth routes - the READ-ONLY config surface rules + rules/history + sites, anonymous GET-only, per the SAME read-only carve-out reasoning REQ-ROC-005 applies to /api/evaluate - so the EXACT expected set is now health decisions evaluate rules rulesHistory sites and the pin ALSO asserts that no rules/sites route carries a non-GET verb (a write route cannot arrive unnoticed even if nobody enumerated it). DEF-ROC-016 the health handler now owns ONLY the reachability probing and delegates the payload to host/healthHttp so build identity is on every answer - route still GET+anonymous unchanged"]
    configReadHttp["src/host/configReadHttp<br/>UC-088 the DEPLOYED host's HTTP adapters for the config READ surface: RULES_ROUTE + RULES_HISTORY_ROUTE + SITES_ROUTE data-shapes all GET+anonymous (routes rules, rules/history, sites); makeRulesHandler/makeRuleHistoryHandler/makeSitesHandler read the QUERY only and call the ONE shared getRules/getRuleHistory/getSites seam - NO read logic and NO second parse; registerConfigReadRoutes(app getRulesDeps getSitesDeps) so each registration NAME/method/authLevel is assertable without the Functions runtime and the reads-only boundary is enforced in ONE place; failure taxonomy: a missing query param = caller-data 400 with the EXISTING local message, a refused config-table read is handled INSIDE the shared seams (UC-086/087 degrade to the seeded baseline + in-band rulesDegraded/draftsUnavailable/historyUnavailable + a categorised external-availability line) so the answer is a USABLE FLAGGED 200 never a dead 503 and never a silent one, and anything the seams do NOT own is still a categorised 503; ?scope=template is REFUSED with an explicit 400 - getTemplateRules is a deliberately NON-fail-safe read (AC-086-5) so serving it would reintroduce the 503 this slice removes and answering the SITE read instead would be the DEF-ROC-013 wrong-answer-that-looks-fine"]
    configReadForHost["src/host/configReadForHost<br/>UC-088 the CLOUD composition roots for the config READ surface - the deployed twins of read-api's makeRulesDeps and makeSitesDeps field for field: composeRulesDeps = RuleConfig store + SEEDED_RULES baseline + seededSiteTemplateOf; composeSitesDeps = SitePatternConfig store + SEEDED_SITES baseline; reuses composition.ts's defaultRuleConfigStore/defaultSitePatternStore so the cloud Config screen and the live consumer share ONE store-auth decision (EXP-047, the same seams UC-084 proves live); lazyRulesDeps/lazySitesDeps memoise on FIRST REQUEST so host import touches no store and a cold start / health probe cannot be broken by table reachability; siteTemplateOf is DELIBERATELY the SEEDED resolver not the store-backed one - it mirrors read-api exactly (a cloud-only divergence would be the DEF-ROC-005 hazard) and it resolves selfManaged/editable with NO store read so a degraded read can never WIDEN what a user may edit (UC-086's guarantee); the EVALUATION path is different and unchanged - evaluateForHost still resolves the parent per request through the store-backed resolver (UC-074); no allocationFloor and no write path is composed here - allocateRuleId is a WRITE this host does not register; DEPLOYED AUTH SHAPE: TABLESTORAGE_ENDPOINT is set so both stores select MANAGED IDENTITY whose grant covers AlertDecisions ONLY today so both config reads are refused until platform Ask A - which is exactly why UC-086/087 landed FIRST: these routes answer a flagged baseline 200 now and the real published data the moment the grant lands NO redeploy either way"]
    healthHttp["src/host/healthHttp<br/>DEF-ROC-016 NEW the /api/health PAYLOAD seam for the deployed host: healthResponse(checks,env) -> status 200/503 + jsonBody ok/serviceBus/eventHubs/topic/subscription/eventHub/consumerGroup + APPENDED buildSha + the x-roc-build response header. Split out from azure-functions so the shape is pinnable with NO live Azure - the deployed endpoint previously carried NO build identity at all so no deployed-environment verdict could be tied to a commit and UC-075 had to be validated by commit-ancestry inference. Identity is reported on the UNHEALTHY 503 too - is-the-fix-live-yet is asked when things are down. MINIMAL BY MANDATE: REQ-ROC-005 AC-1 exempts /health + /api/health from the whole-host auth policy so the deploy pipeline can curl them unauthenticated, so the key SET and the single response header are pinned EXACTLY and the pipeline's own assertion is read out of deploy-ROC.yml by the test rather than remembered"]
    hostJira["src/host/jiraForHost<br/>UC-024 the COMPOSITION-ROOT Jira selection - KEY_VAULT_URI set -> the REAL JiraApiAdapter over the KeyVault SecretPort, unset -> delegate to selectJira (LOCAL fake/JsonFile). DEF-ROC-021 makes two changes at this seam. (1) ROC_JIRA_REAL now gates the KEY VAULT branch TOO: it used to be consulted on the LOCAL branch ONLY so on the deployed host the flag was INERT - setting it false did NOT turn the cloud egress off and did NOT restore service during the 2026-08-05 outage, and anyone reading that app setting was misled about the deployed posture. Off on the cloud path REFUSES (see unavailableJira) - never the fake, because a fake reports success. (2) NEW selectHostJiraResult - the FAIL-SAFE twin the composition root actually calls: any construction failure is caught, classified to a reason CODE, logged once as jira.host.degraded with the taxonomy category + degradedTo:unavailable-egress, recorded for /api/health, and returned IN BAND as degraded/degradeCode/degradeReason with an UnavailableJiraAdapter - it NEVER throws. The STRICT selectHostJira is UNCHANGED and still fails closed on a non-sanctioned tenant; only what the composition root DOES with that refusal changed. THE BOUNDARY IS CONSTRUCTION not the raise: degrading a raise would lose the signal that the ticket did not happen - the same split DEF-ROC-017 drew between a fail-safe READ and a strict WRITE"]
