    buildIdentity["src/host/buildIdentity<br/>DEF-ROC-016 NEW the ONE resolution of which-commit-is-this: buildSha(env) = BUILD_SHA the app setting the DEPLOY PIPELINE stamps from github.sha (Terraform emits it for the dev/prod estates) then ROC_COMMIT_SHA the LOCAL/legacy name then the explicit unknown marker. NEVER a committed constant - a hand-maintained sha drifts from the code it identifies which is worse than nothing. BLANK IS UNKNOWN and the value is TRIMMED: ?? does not catch an empty string so an un-hardened resolver answers buildSha:'' which looks like an answer. Own module so healthHttp resolves identity without pulling the whole composition root; composition.ts RE-EXPORTS it so host.start logging, the Jira commitSha stamp, the rule-version recordedBy attribution and local/read-api all resolve the SAME function - local and deployed cannot report differently"]
