    webProxy["dashboard/server.mjs<br/>DEF-ROC-018 the DEPLOYED WEB TIER and the ONLY caller of the Function App: static dist/ bundle + own anonymous /health + reverse proxy for /api/* -> PPS_EVENT_AGGREGATION_FUNCTION_ORIGIN. WAS fetch target {method signal} - forwarded ONLY the method so NO headers and NO body reached the Function App: a cut-over trap that would derive authenticated:false for every signed-in user and deliver every POST write bodyless the moment Easy Auth Ask D landed runbook E-AU-09. NOW forwards by ALLOWLIST FORWARDED_REQUEST_HEADERS = x-ms-client-principal + content-type ONLY - a PULL over the frozen set never a copy of the incoming bag so a client-forged x-roc-role/x-roc-user CANNOT traverse the hop which is the bypass UC-081 AC-4-HARD exists to prevent; body buffered bounded MAX_PROXIED_BODY_BYTES 1MiB -> 413 caller-data before the upstream hop; failure taxonomy unconfigured-origin 503 internal-configuration + unreachable-upstream 502 external-availability-internal-service both structured-logged for the runbook. Listening moved behind an entrypoint guard so the real artifact is drivable by tests - pinned by spawning node server.mjs. DEF-ROC-016 lands the RESPONSE direction DEF-ROC-018 scoped out: ECHOED_RESPONSE_HEADERS = x-roc-build ONLY pulled from the upstream response by the SAME pullHeaders construction as the request side so neither direction can become a filter - the Function App now sets it so the allowlist no longer forwards a header nothing emits; content-type+cache-control are the proxy's OWN not echoes; the request direction is UNCHANGED (a client-supplied x-roc-build is still dropped) and the x-roc-role forgery source pin was NARROWED to no-x-roc-literal-outside-the-echo-declaration never removed"]

