e ticket attempt, so a refused create escaped handleEvent and the event was recorded NOWHERE. MEASURED LIVE 2026-08-29 on the deployed host: `Jira newtype rejected the request (HTTP 400)` at consumer/index.js:434, invocation Failed, and the Event Hubs checkpoint then ADVANCED PAST IT - never re-delivered across four host restarts, so the throw-and-transport-redelivers posture DEF-ROC-049 relied on IS FALSE ON THIS TRANSPORT and a throw is silent permanent loss, plus (cardinality many, MaxEventBatchSize 100) every REMAINING message of the batch. NOW: alertState.append runs FIRST, before any egress - safe here and ONLY here among the raise-like sites because the ticket idempotency key is the __unrecognised__ MARKER not the record (the record carries no jiraKey and nothing reads it to decide a raise), which is exactly the distinction domain/resolveLease states when it FORBIDS the same reordering for a resolve; and a refusal no retry can change (400/401/403/404) is SAID once per attempt as NewMessageTypeTicketAbandoned reason=create-refused-permanently with the marker given back, NOT thrown, while 408/429 still PROPAGATE unchanged (AC-144.3)"]:::def144changed
    soakSweep["functions/soakSweep<br/>UC-049 createSoakSweep pass: listExpiredHolds now -> per hold re-fold+decideSoakExpiry -> claimSoakExpiry BEFORE createAlert -> append `raised`+jiraKey; skip/claimLost/failed counts; DEF-ROC-049 THE ORDERING CURE: the claim is STILL taken before the create (it is what makes the raise at-most-once) but is now GIVEN BACK when the create PROVABLY did not happen (classifyCreateFailure = ticket-not-created), so a 4xx/429 no longer makes the raise structurally IMPOSSIBLE FOR EVER while the catch logs retryable:true - the pre-fix failure presented as SILENCE, measured over 11 passes. NO DOUBLE-RAISE WINDOW OPENS, and this is the property the naive fix breaks: (1) only the claim WINNER reaches the create, so a release can never race a second create; (2) a release happens ONLY where no ticket exists; (3) the DURABLE at-most-once barrier is the appended `raised` record via wouldRaiseNow's fresh-fold gate, NOT the claim - mutation-proven, since taking the claim AFTER the create yields tickets [#quot;ROC-1#quot;,#quot;ROC-2#quot;] for one fault. An UNKNOWN-outcome create (5xx/timeout) KEEPS its claim and becomes a NEW raiseAbandoned count: PERMANENT, signalled ONCE (the kept claim IS the one-time gate - no extra marker keyspace), retryable:false, never thrown, never `failed`; its remedy is HUMAN and is runbook E-CT-11, because ROC will never raise that alert. A failed RELEASE lands in the same count under reason claim-release-failed rather than being dressed as a retry; DEF-ROC-038 delta018 s5.2 NEW deviceUnmappable count for a hold whose DEVICE has no Jira dropdown value - PERMANENT, signalled ONCE via the EXISTING store-side claim primitive under its OWN ::device-unmappable suffix, NEVER retried, NEVER thrown, NEVER `failed` (which promises a next-tick retry that cannot be kept); kept SEPARATE from identityRejected because the two permanent skips have DIFFERENT remedies (Jira dropdown enum vs the mandatory-field/storage-key contract) and