-claim suffix while the COUNT keeps flagging every pass, runbook E-CT-12; that indistinguishability from a benign overlap is exactly HOW the fault hid, and what remains detectable is the residual DEF-ROC-049s cure leaves standing ON PURPOSE - an UNKNOWN-outcome create keeps its claim rather than risk a SECOND real ticket for one fault; (b) raiseBatchSize on EVERY pass plus one named raise_batch_tripwire line above 25, which is the STATED REVERSAL CONDITION for a bounded per-pass raise budget - no budget is built now, deliberately; (c) oldest_open_hold_age_s with its budget applied PER HOLD as heldUntil-eventTs + 2x pollInterval, so a correctly window-extended hold reads CLEAN where the old delay-only budget would have flagged CORRECT behaviour, computed tolerantly OUTSIDE the per-candidate catch so one poison instant cannot cost the pass its raises. pollIntervalMs is the detectors only input and its ABSENCE IS LOUD - orphan_detector_unconfigured, never a quiet degrade to claimLost"]
