    decisionRecord["domain/decisionRecord<br/>DecisionRecord v0 + buildDecisionRecord site/outcome/heldUntil + foldAlertState (UC-048 soak-aware: total order (eventTs,messageId~RowKey), surfaces heldUntil, de-bounced arbitrates over co-present soak-expiry raised) + decideRecovery + UC-048 decideDeBounce (held-until in-window clear eventTs<=heldUntil inclusive); DEF-ROC-029 delta016 makes the DECISIONS order-insensitive too (the STATE fold already was): NEW `cleared` outcome (still schemaVersion 0 - one enum member, no new field); foldAlertState now terminalises on LIFECYCLE outcomes ONLY (raised/held-until/resolved/de-bounced/suppressed-until/cleared) while recognised/unrecognised/not-handled AND any unknown future outcome are carried+counted but can NEVER terminalise - the mask, pinned shut; a partition with NO lifecycle record folds exactly as before (back-compat); the lifecycle walk DERIVES `de-bounced` from an in-window `cleared` (eventTs<=heldUntil inclusive) so delta 007 invariant 2 rests on a RECORD not on the masking accident - THE TRAP: making lifecycle records win WITHOUT this derivation would flip that case from accidentally-right to a FALSE ticket; surfaces pendingClearTs (TERMINAL-relative per events/catalog: an unconsumed clear against an OPEN raised/held-until terminal) for the sweep's resolve legs; NEW decideLateRecovery reads the LOG not the terminal (deliberate deviation from the delta sketch, justified in-source: pendingClearTs is superseded by a later raise, which loses the clear SANDWICHED between two faults that AC-1's 6 three-event permutations need) and returns the {faultId}::late-resolve key; FORWARD-MAP RULE: a stored `recognised` is NEVER re-read as a clear so replay fires no resolve storm; AC-8 STRUCTURAL PIN: OUTCOME_CLASSIFICATION is Record<DecisionOutcome,...> so an unclassified future outcome is a COMPILE failure, plus a `never` default in the lifecycle walk"]
