    alertPayload["domain/alertPayload<br/>build CreateAlertInput + ADF; UC-078 the alertStatus it is GIVEN is now the classified status so the derived summary + ADF description name the real fault too; DEF-ROC-114 it NO LONGER takes a pre-narrowed alertStatus - its input is the OBSERVED status the fault occurred under and it DERIVES BOTH surfaces here: the free-text summary/description name the fault via toAlertSummaryStatus while customfield_12074 is narrowed to a valid dropdown option via toAlertStatusField. The two used to be ONE input so the free text inherited the DROPDOWNs constraint and an ERROR fault - the one raisable fault with no dropdown option - raised a ticket reading Unknown alert on device BGR live ROC-25, asserting a DIFFERENT REAL STATUS since Unknown is itself a vocabulary member. One input two derived surfaces = a caller CANNOT make them disagree and CANNOT lose the fault by narrowing too early EXP-047; when they diverge the ADF says so explicitly naming both so P5 is never left choosing between two statuses on one ticket"]
