    evaluateTrace["domain/evaluateTrace<br/>UC-032 evaluateWithTrace: site resolution override/pattern/unconfigured + walk EVERY effective rule won/lost/skipped disabled|expired/no-match+failing dim; winner FROM decideForSite so cannot drift; outcomes raised/suppressed/not-handled/not-evaluated/held-until DEF-005: alert+delay>0 HELDS parity w/pipeline, heldUntil=eventTs+delay via addSecondsUtc only when time supplied; NO de-bounced; DEF-ROC-015 now APPLIES the SHARED fault gate faultStatus.isFaultStatus imported never re-implemented in the SAME stage order the pipeline uses site-derivation THEN gate - a recognised NON-fault status is never rule-evaluated by decideRules so it is never rule-evaluated here either -> outcome not-evaluated with an EMPTY trace and no winner; it previously walked the rule set and reported raised-via-fallback for OK/OPEN i.e. a confident wrong answer on the surface a rules owner uses to decide whether a config change is safe to publish DEF-ROC-005 drift family; not-evaluated is deliberately DISTINCT from not-handled unconfigured site - two different causes the reader must tell apart"]
    soakExpiry["domain/soakExpiry<br/>UC-049 PURE decideSoakExpiry held,fold,now: raise IFF fold STILL held-until for THIS hold no intervening clear/de-bounce/raise AND now>=heldUntil; synthetic raise messageId=holdId::soak-expiry, eventTs=ORIGINAL fault time so Actual-start=fault time not sweep clock; alert built from held event data; tolerant of unknown fold outcome; DEF-ROC-038 delta018 s5.2 THE `?? held.device` RAW-VALUE FALLBACK IS GONE: it made a hold on a device with no Jira dropdown value return a COMPLETE alert (device XXXX, summary Paper Out alert on device XXXX at UYD1BD01) which assertDropdown threw 400 on, counted `failed` = retried-next-tick, for a candidate that can NEVER succeed - an error line every tick for ever. The raise gate is factored into ONE shared wouldRaiseNow consumed by BOTH decideSoakExpiry and the NEW pure decideSoakExpiryPermanentSkip, so the raise and the permanent skip are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE by construction and the skip can never be claimed for a hold the fold already arbitrated away (that stays a normal skipped); device resolution is now the TOTAL deviceEnumGuard so a `?? raw` fallback is not expressible; DEF-ROC-029 delta016: the guard now reads the fold's LIFECYCLE terminal instead of relying on the masking accident (a plain `recognised` clear used to mask the hold, so this returned null and the alert was DROPPED SILENTLY - Finding C, the whole defect); decideSoakExpiry additionally carries pendingClearTs + a resolveRecordDraft when the recovery is already known so the host can raise-then-resolve; NEW pure decidePendingResolve for the sweep's resolve-only retry leg (terminal `raised` + pendingClearTs + a jiraKey); resolve drafts use the deterministic {holdId}::soak-resolve RowKey; UC-ROC-097 delta019 adds the two PURE derivations the sweeps delta-019 obligations need, both read off the FROZEN heldUntil so neither needs the window: decideOrphanedClaim - gated on the SAME shared wouldRaiseNow as the raise itself, so it can only fire for a hold that would OTHERWISE HAVE RAISED and never for one the fold already arbitrated away - and openHoldAgeBudgetMs/oldestOpenHoldAge, the per-hold age budget heldUntil-eventTs + soakGraceMs, tolerant of an unparseable instant because it runs once per pass outside the per-candidate catch. soakGraceMs is the ONE definition of the 2-poll-interval grace shared by both"]
    resolveLease["domain/resolveLease<br/>DEF-ROC-104 NEW PURE resolveLeaseKey node,device,issueKey,recoveredEventTs -> one key per RESOLVE FACT plus ::resolve-lease suffix. WHY IT EXISTS: every leg that resolves a PPSM Alert decides from a fold READ and then makes an EXTERNAL NON-IDEMPOTENT jira.resolveAlert call BEFORE its own `resolved` record lands, so two legs whose reads straddle that ~1.7s window BOTH conclude the resolve is owed and ONE fault is resolved TWICE - measured deterministically 8/8 red pre-fix in tests/unit/def104OverlappingSweepResolve + 3/3 red over real Azurite in tests/acceptance/def104-overlapping-resolve-azurite, and it is what reddened def029 AC-4 in CI which - being a needs: of deploy-test - SKIPPED the deploy (DEF-ROC-086 signature) and held the environment behind trunk. NOT AN ORDER CHANGE: appending `resolved` first and letting insert-if-not-exists pick the winner is the FORBIDDEN DEF-ROC-049 shape - the record would establish the resolve idempotency key BEFORE the Jira call, so a failed call leaves the log saying `resolved` with the ticket OPEN, the fold consumes the pending clear and nothing ever retries. NOT AN INVARIANT EITHER: DEF-ROC-093 closed its sibling race with an order-independent invariant re-derived AFTER append, which can only REPAIR - a second Jira resolve cannot be un-made, so at-most-once on an external effect can only be settled by an atomic store op taken BEFORE the call. KEYED ON THE FACT NOT THE LEG, so either leg derives the same key and they CONVERGE, and a genuinely different resolve (later incident, later recovery instant) is a different fact never blocked by a stale one. Derived never stored - nothing to keep in step (EXP-047). ALWAYS RELEASED, success and failure alike: it guards only the in-flight window and the DURABLE at-most-once authority stays the appended `resolved` record + the fold, so the fail-safe direction is OPEN - unlike a raise claim (DEF-ROC-049 keeps it, a duplicate raise is a second real Alert) a resolve never retried leaves an OPEN ticket for a recovered device, which since DEF-ROC-093 also SUPPRESSES the next genuine raise = SILENCE, the worst outcome an alerting system has. RESIDUAL STATED: a host dying INSIDE the Jira call leaks its lease, observable not silent - the hold stays a candidate so soak.sweep.resolve_lease_lost logs on EVERY later pass; a count that PERSISTS is a leak, one that stops was the benign overlap."]:::def104changed
    canonicalRuleHash["domain/canonicalRuleHash<br/>UC-056 PURE sha256 of a rule's evaluation/identity fields node/devices-set/statuses-set/priority/enabled/action/delay/until + id/scope/site; membership order-independent; cosmetic name change invariant; groundwork for UC-057/058 attestation gate; node:crypto only, cloud-agnostic. DEF-ROC-051/052: unrenderableEventTimeDetail is now EXPORTED because it IS the calendar arithmetic and two further sites were using Number.isNaN(Date.parse(x)) as a calendar check - a rule draft's until and the ?since= query parameter. They consume it through calendarDate. No behaviour change here; the export is what stops a THIRD copy of the leap-year rule"]
    identityKey["domain/alertIdentityKey<br/>DEF-ROC-030 NEW - the ONE place that decides whether a payload-derived value may become a STORAGE KEY. node/device/messageId arrive from PPSM Computer/Device/Id and were used UNVALIDATED as PartitionKey=node|device and RowKey=ticksD19|messageId: a forbidden char / \\ # ? or control char 0x00-0x1F/0x7F-0x9F or an over-1024-char key gave a 400 on append -> throwing consumer -> Event Hubs redelivery -> the event NEVER recorded (silent loss, same family as DEF-ROC-022/031), and `|` being the identity separator let node=A device=B|C FORGE the partition of node=A|B device=C (cross-device read+write, NO error at all). validateStorageKeyParts REJECTS - never normalises/truncates, because mangling can merge two distinct devices into ONE alert identity which is silent and unrecoverable where a rejection is visible and recoverable; rejecting the separator in node/device is what makes the partition key INJECTIVE on its accepted domain. AUTHORISED SET ONLY (v140 s17h): the engineer implemented exactly what security/table-storage-alert-state.md authorised and ESCALATED the rest, correctly. RULED IN DELTA 017: (1) an EMPTY/whitespace node or device is now OUT of the domain - the injectivity reasoning that admitted it was RIGHT but about the wrong arrow, since an empty segment breaks IDENTITY EXTRACTION one step UPSTREAM of the key (many devices map onto one pair BEFORE the key function is called), so a key-inspecting validator structurally cannot see the merge; MEASURED through the real delta-016 fold - a gate reader's ONLINE RESOLVED a printer's open PAPER OUT ticket, and 3 faults on one blank identity left 2 tickets permanently unresolvable (the fold has ONE jiraIssueKey slot). New reason `empty`, same quarantine lane, counted SEPARATELY because its remedy is the mandatory-field contract not a character-set widening. (2) the separator IS still allowed in messageId but the REASON IS CORRECTED: not 'the D19 prefix is fixed-width' (padStart pads and never truncates, so it bounds nothing - the 19-digit cap actually comes from actualStart.ts's FOUR-DIGIT-YEAR regex TWO MODULES AWAY, which nothing pins) but 'the prefix CANNOT CONTAIN THE SEPARATOR, so the FIRST separator is always the split, whatever the width' - unconditional, and the invariant the pin must assert. (3) an EMPTY messageId is IN the domain: the SB source already nominates sequenceNumber as the fallback, `??` just misses blank; blank makes the RowKey non-discriminating at MS resolution so the 412 silently swallows a DIFFERENT event. (4) STILL OPEN, sibling defect - eventTs is the FOURTH payload-derived key input and is NOT validated: a calendar-invalid `created` (2026-13-45 passes normalise's shape-only regex) THROWS inside ticksD19 AFTER this gate -> throwing consumer -> EH redelivery -> event NEVER recorded, this defect's headline failure mode still live. Also owns the RESERVED quarantine identity __malformed_identity__|rejected + malformedIdentityRecord (raw values preserved VERBATIM in the payload, sha256 messageId so it is deterministic/bounded/key-safe -> a redelivery is an insert-only no-op) + malformedIdentityLogFields (category malformed-identity, states the CONSEQUENCE, makes NO health claim about the population it counts); node:crypto only, cloud-agnostic<br/>DEF-ROC-055 - unrenderableEventTimeDetail is now ALSO the pipeline's instant gate (imported, never re-derived), so the shape arm and the calendar arm are ONE rejection with ONE reason; and malformedIdentityLogFields now escapes/bounds eventTs on the log line, because a carried-through created is untrusted publisher text of unbounded length"]
