    ruleDraft["domain/ruleDraft<br/>UC-056 RuleDraft = unpublished editable Rule for a self-managed site + validateDraftRule AUTHORITATIVE well-formedness gate: exactly one alert/suppress, delay 0-86400, priority 0-1000, compilable node glob, non-empty/ANY dims, until only-on-suppress, accumulates errors; 400-never-persisted P3 guard; UC-059 newRuleDraftTemplate(id,site) = the ONE fresh-draft shape well-formed defaults scope:site. DEF-ROC-051 REDIRECTS the until check: it was Number.isNaN(Date.parse(until)) which is NOT a calendar check - Date.parse rejects an out-of-range month but SILENTLY ROLLS OVER an out-of-range day or hour, so until 2026-02-30 was ACCEPTED and quietly meant 2 March and until 2026-02-29 in the non-leap 2026 was NOT expired on 28 Feb but WAS expired on 1 Mar (measured through the real validateDraftRule + suppressionExpired). until decides when a suppress rule STOPS governing whether a real fault raises a ticket and is authored by a NON-ENGINEER in the C4 config UI, so a rule silently stopped or kept applying on a day nobody chose. Now delegates to calendarDate for BOTH validateDraftRule and validateTemplateDraftRule via the shared validateCommonRuleFields - one gate, both authoring surfaces - and holds NO Date.parse / new Date at all, by source-level pin"]
    calendarDate["domain/calendarDate<br/>DEF-ROC-051 + DEF-ROC-052 NEW - calendar validity for an AUTHORED or QUERIED date. It DOES NOT re-derive the calendar: the leap-year rule and the month-length table stay in exactly ONE place, identityKey.unrenderableEventTimeDetail built and measured under DEF-ROC-034, which this delegates to (EXP-047 one fact one writer - a second copy is how the predicate and the render drifted apart in the first place). All it adds is tolerance of a date-ONLY YYYY-MM-DD value, which the DEF-ROC-034 site never sees because an eventTs always carries a time, plus the caller-facing message so every surface words the rejection identically. DECLARES the accepted set as a constant AND as an executable corpus tests/fixtures/calendar-validity-corpus.json which the dashboard MIRROR of this control asserts against too - the two are separate compilation units and cannot import each other, so the corpus is what stops them drifting. Deliberately NARROWER than Date.parse: the non-ISO spellings it swallowed - 2026-8-1, 2026/08/01, 1 August 2026 - are implementation-defined AND parsed as LOCAL time, a second silent reinterpretation a whole day out west of Greenwich. Exports InvalidCalendarDateError, a NAMED 4xx-class error so the HTTP surfaces map it to a 400 by instanceof rather than by sniffing a message prefix. PURE, no clock, no I-O, no SDK"]
    loadEffectiveRules["domain/loadEffectiveRules<br/>UC-056 the ONE shared read path DEF-005/EXP-047: foldPublishedVersions latest-ticks-per-ruleId + mergeEffectiveCatalogue published-overrides-baseline + effectiveRuleSet ordering; async loadEffectiveRules reads store per-call no-redeploy pickup; UC-058 adds loadEffectiveCatalogue the shared merged catalogue both pipeline decideRules + Simulator evaluateApi fold, cannot drift AC-058-5; DEF-ROC-017 FAIL-SAFE: loadEffectiveCatalogueForSite now catches a store-read failure refused/unavailable/unprovisioned RuleConfig and returns the BASELINE floor instead of throwing - the SAME posture the two sibling config reads already take loadEffectiveSitePatterns -> SEEDED_SITES + makeSiteTemplateLinkResolver.load -> seeded link map so all three degrade identically; NOT silent: a categorised external-availability line naming iata+scope+scopeId+degradedTo:baseline PLUS an in-band status via loadEffectiveCatalogueForSiteResult that the Simulator surfaces as body.rulesDegraded; READS ONLY - loadEffectiveCatalogueForSiteStrict still THROWS and is what the WRITE/attestation path relinkPreview/breakSnapshotForSite uses so an unreachable store can never be attested to or persisted as the template's published rules; UC-086 extends the SAME split to the ORDERED per-site read the ADMIN surface uses: NEW loadEffectiveRulesResult degrades to the baseline's effective set + logs external-availability op:loadEffectiveRules scope+scopeId+degradedTo:baseline + reports degradedToBaseline IN BAND while loadEffectiveRules stays the STRICT twin that PROPAGATES - both now compose the ONE orderedEffectiveSet derivation so the strict and fail-safe twins can differ ONLY in what they do with a FAILURE never in the answer"]
    loadEffectiveSitePatterns["domain/loadEffectiveSitePatterns<br/>UC-066 the ONE shared SITE read path DEF-005/EXP-047 mirror of loadEffectiveRules keyed by IATA: foldPublishedSitePatterns latest-ticks-per-IATA poison-pattern-skip + mergeEffectiveSites published-overrides-baseline; reads siteStore per-call no-redeploy pickup AC-066-3; BOTH pipeline sitesFor via readThroughSitesFor AND Simulator evaluateApi fold it, cannot drift AC-066-4; FAIL-SAFE: unavailable/virgin store -> SEEDED_SITES floor, NEVER empty site list"]
    publishGate["domain/publishGate<br/>UC-058 PURE by-construction publish gate AC-058-2/CC-5: evaluatePublishGate recompute canonicalRuleHash==submitted hash-mismatch else, attestation exists for that hash no-attestation else, fresh within freshness window stale-attestation else; content-hash-bound timing-independent; no store/IO cloud-agnostic"]
    templatePublishGate["domain/templatePublishGate<br/>UC-069 PURE DUAL by-construction template publish gate AC-069-1/2/4/5 CC-T5/T7: evaluateTemplatePublishGate requires submitted-hash==canonicalRuleHash(draft) hash-mismatch else, a FRESH __ruledrafttest__ attestation no-attestation/stale-attestation else, AND a FRESH __templateblastconfirm__ confirmation whose linkedSitesHash==current no-confirmation/stale-linkset/stale-confirmation else; fail-CLOSED under-report is the J16 failure; content-hash+linkset-hash bound; no store/IO cloud-agnostic; reused VERBATIM by UC-070 publish EXECUTION"]
    canonicalLinkedSitesHash["domain/canonicalLinkedSitesHash<br/>UC-069 PURE sha256 of the SORTED linked-site IATA list; deterministic order-independent; the link-dimension content key __templateblastconfirm__ binds to (CC-T7 a link/unlink stales the confirmation); empty-list has its own stable hash AC-069-6; node:crypto only cloud-agnostic"]
    selectRuleConfigStore["config/selectRuleConfigStore<br/>UC-058 RuleConfig AUTH SELECTION seam mirror of selectAlertStore; TABLESTORAGE_ENDPOINT set DEV/PROD -> MI shape endpoint+ROC/TABLESTORAGE_RULECONFIG_TABLE_NAME default RuleConfig same storage-account family; unset LOCAL -> connection-string Azurite; DefaultAzureCredential no network at construction; composition defaultRuleConfigStore calls it for the consumer pickup loader"]
    selectSitePatternStore["config/selectSitePatternStore<br/>UC-064 SitePatternConfig AUTH SELECTION seam mirror of selectRuleConfigStore; TABLESTORAGE_ENDPOINT set DEV/PROD -> MI shape endpoint+ROC/TABLESTORAGE_SITEPATTERN_TABLE_NAME default SitePatternConfig same storage-account family; unset LOCAL -> connection-string Azurite; DefaultAzureCredential no network at construction"]

    %% adapters implement ports
    sbSource -->|"implements"| telPort
    ehProducer -->|"implements"| logProdPort
    ehConsumer -->|"implements"| logConsPort
    fakeJira -->|"implements"| jiraPort
    jiraApi -->|"implements"| jiraPort
    jiraApi --> secretPort
    unavailableJira -->|"implements"| jiraPort
    tableStore -->|"implements"| alertStatePort
    tableStoreQuery -->|"implements"| decisionLogQueryPort
    envSecret -->|"implements"| secretPort
    jsonSecret -->|"implements"| secretPort
    kvSecret -->|"implements"| secretPort

    %% UC-ROC-018 SecretPort selection seam: KEY_VAULT_URI set -> KeyVaultSecretAdapter
    %% (DEV/PROD via managed identity), unset -> EnvSecretAdapter (LOCAL, unchanged).
    selectSecret --> kvSecret
    selectSecret --> envSecret

    %% UC-ROC-019 ServiceBus auth selection seam: SERVICEBUS_NAMESPACE_FQDN set ->
    %% managed-identity shape (DEV/PROD), unset -> connection-string shape (LOCAL).
    selectSbSource --> sbSource

    %% UC-ROC-020 Event Hubs auth selection seam: EVENTHUB_NAMESPACE_FQDN set ->
    %% managed-identity shape (DEV/PROD), unset -> connection-string shape (LOCAL).
    %% One seam feeds BOTH EH adapters (producer + consumer).
    selectEh --> ehProducer
    selectEh --> ehConsumer
    %% DEF-ROC-112 — the ACTUAL runtime routing path, previously UNMARKED: every deployed
    %% event crosses this converter on its way from the Functions trigger to the handler.
    hostInvocation -->|"feeds RawTelemetryMessage"| forwarder
    hostInvocation -->|"feeds RawTelemetryMessage"| consumer

    %% UC-ROC-025 Table Storage auth selection seam: TABLESTORAGE_ENDPOINT set ->
    %% managed-identity TableClient, unset -> connection-string/Azurite.
    selectAlertStore --> tableStore

    %% UC-ROC-016 selection seam: the factory constructs ONE of the two Jira
    %% adapters (default fake) and, on the real path, the JSON-file secret source.
    selectJira --> fakeJira
    selectJira --> jiraApi
    selectJira --> jsonSecret

    %% UC-ROC-024 / DEF-ROC-021 — the HOST Jira seam. `hostJira` chooses the cloud
    %% (Key Vault) credential path or delegates to the LOCAL `selectJira`, and its
    %% FAIL-SAFE twin substitutes `unavailableJira` when the real adapter cannot be
    %% CONSTRUCTED, so the composition root below still yields a working pipeline.
    %% The posture it resolves is recorded for the one reachable surface we have.
    hostJira --> selectJira
    hostJira --> selectSecret
    hostJira --> jiraApi
    hostJira --> unavailableJira
    hostJira --> jiraEgressStatus
    soakPollerHost --> hostJira
    jiraEgressStatus --> selectJira
    %% DEF-ROC-021: `/api/health` is the ONLY reachable observability surface (Kudu /
    %% log-streaming is blocked by IP policy — runbook E-AU-07), so the health payload
    %% seam reports the egress posture. It NEVER feeds `ok`: healthCheckPath drives
    %% instance rotation, which is what amplified the original 502 into an outage.
    healthHttp --> jiraEgressStatus

    %% DEF-ROC-012: the LOCAL PIPELINE entrypoints (local/demo + local/soak-poller,
    %% the latter inside soakPollerHost) apply the committed dev profile to
    %% process.env BEFORE composing, so the dev composed stack resolves the REAL
    %% egress through the UNCHANGED selectJira / selectHostJira seam. Config edge —
    %% devProfile is not imported BY the seam; it supplies the env the seam reads.
    soakPollerHost --> devProfile
    devProfile -.->|"sets ROC_JIRA_REAL in dev"| selectJira

    %% DEF-ROC-019: the two REASONS to drive the pipeline are now two entrypoints over
    %% ONE shared body. Only the WATCH side reaches the real egress, and it is wired to
    %% the teardown reconciliation in the same breath — the seeder cannot reach either.
    localDemoSeed --> devProfile
    localDemoSeed --> selectJira
    localDemoSeed --> localDemoRun
    localDemoWatch --> devProfile
    localDemoWatch --> selectJira
    localDemoWatch --> trackedEgress
    localDemoWatch --> demoTeardownRun
    localDemoWatch --> localDemoRun
    trackedEgress -->|"implements"| jiraPort
    localDemoRun --> forwarder
    localDemoRun --> consumer
    localDemoRun --> soakPollerHost
    localDemoRun --> jiraPort

    %% ISOLATED demo egress (UC-ROC-053) — a SEPARATE selection path; shares no
    %% flag/file with selectJira. demoEgress decorates the selected JiraPort.
    demoEgress -->|"implements"| jiraPort
    demoEgress --> demoRegistry
    selectDemoJira --> fakeJira
    selectDemoJira --> jiraApi
    selectDemoJira --> jsonSecret
    localDemoTeardown --> selectDemoJira
    localDemoTeardown --> demoTeardownRun
    localDemoTeardown --> demoRegistry
    demoTeardownRun --> jiraPort
    demoClassify --> selectDemoJira

    %% Living-demo SCENARIO drivers (UC-ROC-080). scenarioHarness is the ONE
    %% composition both drivers go through, so neither can compose the pipeline
    %% differently. The status driver reads the catalogue for WHAT to inject and the
    %% committed capture record for the ENVELOPE it rides on.
    scenarioHarness --> selectDemoJira
    scenarioHarness --> demoEgress
    scenarioHarness --> demoRegistry
    scenarioHarness --> tableStore
    scenarioHarness --> pipeline
    scenarioDrive --> scenarioHarness
    scenarioDrive --> statusScenarioDrive
    scenarioDrive --> consumer
    scenarioDrive --> demoRegistry
    scenarioDrive --> decisionRecord
    statusScenarios --> normalise
    statusScenarioDrive --> statusScenarios
    statusScenarioDrive --> scenarioHarness
    statusScenarioDrive --> consumer
    statusScenarioDrive --> decisionRecord
    statusScenarioDrive --> deviceCode
    statusScenarioDrive --> demoRegistry
    statusScenarioList --> statusScenarios

    %% UC-ROC-017 live acceptance harness wiring: selects the real adapter via the
    %% UC-016 seam, wires it into the real pipeline (forwarder+consumer) to raise
    %% ONE ticket, verifies via the diagnostic read-back, tears down (selected
    %% JiraPort.teardownAlert), and re-reads to confirm statusCategory==done.
    jiraReadBack --> secretPort
    uc017Harness --> selectJira
    uc017Harness --> jiraReadBack
    uc017Harness --> jsonSecret
    uc017Harness --> jiraPort
    uc017Harness --> consumer
    uc017Harness --> forwarder
    uc017Harness --> alertStatePort

    %% UC-ROC-009 read path: SPA -> HTTP boundary -> query port (adapters depend on domain-defined port)
    readApi --> decisionLogQueryPort
    readApi --> tableStoreQuery
    readApi --> readApiFilter
    %% DEF-ROC-116: the ticket url is derived at the READ BOUNDARY, by BOTH roots,
    %% from ONE app setting read per request — never bundled into the browser
    %% (delta 020 DECISION 1: a bundled destination is stale by construction).
    readApi -->|"jiraUrl per record"| jiraTicketUrl
    azureFunctionsHost -->|"jiraUrl per record"| jiraTicketUrl
    %% DEF-ROC-052: `?since=` was passed through with NO validation at all on this
    %% surface, so a calendar-invalid since silently shifted the window AND an
    %% unparseable one surfaced as a 503 (availability) instead of a caller-data 400.
    readApiFilter --> calendarDate
    readApi -->|"400 on InvalidCalendarDateError"| calendarDate
    readApi --> evaluateApi
    %% UC-084: the SECOND composition root over the SAME seam (the deployed host).
    %% DEF-ROC-052: the deployed decisions route validated `?since=` with
    %% Number.isNaN(Date.parse(since)), so ?since=2026-02-30 returned a valid-looking
    %% 200 for a window starting 2 March - the worst of the three outcomes because the
    %% caller has no signal and the data looks correct. Now a 400 naming field+reason,
    %% mapped by instanceof rather than the old message-prefix sniff.
    azureFunctionsHost --> calendarDate
    azureFunctionsHost --> evaluateHttp
    azureFunctionsHost --> evaluateForHost
    %% UC-088: the SECOND composition root over the rules/sites READ seams.
    azureFunctionsHost --> configReadHttp
    azureFunctionsHost --> configReadForHost
    configReadHttp --> rulesApi
    configReadHttp --> sitesApi
    configReadForHost --> soakPollerHost
    configReadForHost --> rules
    configReadForHost --> siteConfig
    %% DEF-ROC-016: build identity, resolved ONCE and reported on every boundary that
    %% can be asked from outside. The four in-edges are the point: a second resolution
    %% would let the host's start log, the deployed health answer and the local dev
    %% server disagree about which commit is running.
    azureFunctionsHost -->|"health payload"| healthHttp
    healthHttp --> buildIdentity
    soakPollerHost -->|"host.start log + recordedBy attribution"| buildIdentity
    readApi -->|"/api/health buildSha + x-roc-build"| buildIdentity
    evaluateHttp --> evaluateApi
    evaluateForHost --> soakPollerHost
    evaluateForHost --> rules
    evaluateForHost --> siteConfig
    evaluateForHost --> siteTemplateLink
    evaluateApi --> evaluateTrace
    evaluateApi --> rules
    evaluateApi --> siteConfig
    evaluateApi --> deviceCode
    evaluateApi --> normalise
    %% UC-058 parity rewire: the Simulator seam folds the SHARED store (loadEffective
    %% Catalogue) instead of SEEDED_RULES, so it reads what the pipeline reads (AC-058-5).
    evaluateApi --> loadEffectiveRules
    evaluateApi --> ruleConfigStorePort
    evaluateApi --> loadEffectiveSitePatterns
    evaluateApi --> sitePatternStorePort
    loadEffectiveSitePatterns --> siteConfig
    loadEffectiveSitePatterns --> sitePatternStorePort
    evaluateTrace --> rulesEngine
    evaluateTrace --> siteConfig
    evaluateTrace --> actualStart
    decisionApi -->|"GET /api/decisions?filter"| readApi
    %% DEF-ROC-018: the ACTUAL DEPLOYED routing path for the SAME relative
    %% `/api/*` fetch the SPA clients issue. Locally it lands on local/read-api
    %% (the edge above, via the vite dev proxy); deployed it lands on the web host,
    %% which forwards the allowlisted headers + the body to the Function App.
    decisionApi -->|"deployed: same-origin /api/*"| webProxy
    webProxy -->|"allowlisted forward: x-ms-client-principal + content-type + body"| azureFunctionsHost
    useDecisions --> decisionApi
    decisionApi --> decisionView
    decisionPage --> decisionView
    decisionPage --> decisionToolbar
    decisionToolbar --> decisionView
    useDecisions --> decisionPage

    %% UC-ROC-056 rules-authoring write path: read-api hosts the rulesApi seam,
    %% which reads/writes the RuleConfig store via the domain-defined port + the
    %% shared loader + the draft validator. Adapters depend on the domain port.
    ruleConfigStore -->|"implements"| ruleConfigStorePort
    canonicalRuleHash --> rulesEngine
    ruleDraft --> rulesEngine
    %% DEF-ROC-051: the authoring-time calendar gate. ONE control, reached by BOTH
    %% validateDraftRule and validateTemplateDraftRule through validateCommonRuleFields.
    ruleDraft --> calendarDate
    %% DEF-ROC-051/052: the calendar ARITHMETIC is not re-derived here - it is the
    %% DEF-ROC-034 instant check, now exported for these two callers.
    calendarDate --> identityKey
    loadEffectiveRules --> rulesEngine
    loadEffectiveRules --> ruleConfigStorePort
    ruleConfigStore --> canonicalRuleHash
    ruleConfigStore --> ruleDraft
    rulesApi --> ruleConfigStorePort
    rulesApi --> ruleDraft
    rulesApi --> loadEffectiveRules
    rulesApi --> ruleVersionDiff
    readApi --> rulesApi
    readApi --> ruleConfigStore
    %% UC-072 relink-preview read wiring (delta 015 Decision 3/5)
    relinkPreview --> loadEffectiveRules
    relinkPreview --> rulesEngine
    relinkPreview --> ruleConfigStorePort
    siteTemplateLinkApi --> relinkPreview
    readApi --> siteTemplateLinkApi
    relinkCommit --> siteTemplateLinkStorePort
    relinkCommit --> ruleConfigStorePort
    relinkCommit --> siteTemplateLink
    relinkCommit --> canonicalRuleHash
    relinkCommit --> relinkPreview
    relinkCommitApi --> relinkCommit
    readApi --> relinkCommitApi
    readApi --> linkResolver
    %% UC-073 relink CONFIRM + the COMMIT gate wiring (delta 015 Decision 4)
    canonicalRelinkPreviewHash --> canonicalRuleHash
    canonicalRelinkPreviewHash --> relinkPreview
    relinkConfirmGate --> ruleConfigStorePort
    relinkConfirmApi --> relinkPreview
    relinkConfirmApi --> canonicalRelinkPreviewHash
    relinkConfirmApi --> relinkConfirmGate
    relinkConfirmApi --> ruleConfigStorePort
    relinkConfirmApi --> siteTemplateLinkApi
    siteTemplateLinkApi --> canonicalRelinkPreviewHash
    relinkCommitApi --> relinkConfirmApi
    readApi --> relinkConfirmApi
    ruleConfigStore --> ruleConfigStorePort
    relinkPage --> relinkClient
    relinkPage --> relinkDomain
    readApi --> rules

    %% UC-ROC-064 site-pattern authoring write path (DRAFT half): read-api hosts
    %% the sitesApi seam (admin-gated) over the NEW SitePatternStorePort/adapter;
    %% siteDraft is the authoritative well-formedness gate; canonicalSitePatternHash
    %% is the idempotency key. ZERO live-pipeline wiring this UC (AC-064-4) — no edge
    %% into pipeline/deriveSite; that arrives with UC-066's publish + loader.
    sitePatternStore -->|"implements"| sitePatternStorePort
    sitePatternStore --> canonicalSitePatternHash
    sitePatternStore --> siteDraft
    siteDraft --> siteConfig
    canonicalSitePatternHash --> siteConfig
    sitesApi --> sitePatternStorePort
    sitesApi --> siteDraft
    sitesApi --> siteConfig
    readApi --> sitesApi
    readApi --> sitePatternStore
    selectSitePatternStore --> sitePatternStore

    %% UC-ROC-068 site<->template LINK registry (delta 014 Decision 1) — a NEW
    %% READ-ONLY port/adapter over the __sitetemplatelink__ partition of the EXISTING
    %% SitePatternConfig table + the single-source link fold. The forward resolver
    %% (seededSiteTemplateOf, DEMOTED to a projection) is re-exported by rules so
    %% pipeline/evaluateTrace/rulesApi resolve the link via the SAME authoritative
    %% fold — no second source (AC-068-3). Read-only; reuses the existing grant
    %% (NO widening); the __sitetemplatelink__ partition is off the hot `sites` fold
    %% so a linked-but-patternless site (BHX) needs no bogus pattern row (AC-068-4).
    siteTemplateLinkStore -->|"implements"| siteTemplateLinkStorePort
    siteTemplateLink --> siteTemplateLinkStorePort
    linkResolver --> siteTemplateLinkStorePort
    linkResolver --> siteTemplateLink
    rules --> siteTemplateLink
    selectSitePatternStore --> siteTemplateLinkStore
    soakPollerHost --> linkResolver
    soakPollerHost --> siteTemplateLinkStore

    %% UC-ROC-065 site-pattern DRAFT-TEST + by-construction publish GATE (still the
    %% DRAFT/gate half — the publish EXECUTION/append/attribution/pickup is UC-066).
    %% sitesApi gains siteDraftTest (match the draft glob over a bounded recent
    %% decision-log node window via the SHARED deriveSite engine -> regressions +
    %% gains; mint the __sitedrafttest__ attestation ONLY when data available,
    %% AC-065-6; read-only wrt the live pipeline, AC-065-5) + sitePublish (the
    %% content-hash gate: reject 409 an untested/edited/stale draft at the write
    %% path, AC-065-4/5). ATTESTATION methods ADDED to sitePatternStorePort/adapter;
    %% listRecentNodes ADDED to decisionLogQueryPort/tableStoreQuery (unscoped recent
    %% window spanning mapped + NOT-HANDLED). STILL no edge into pipeline/deriveSite.
    siteDraftTest --> siteConfig
    sitePublishGate --> canonicalSitePatternHash
    sitesApi --> siteDraftTest
    sitesApi --> sitePublishGate
    sitesApi --> canonicalSitePatternHash

    %% ── DEF-ROC-065 — the authoring screen READS THE FOLD, it no longer re-derives ──
    %% The NEW edge, and it is the whole fix: `sitesApi` now depends on the SHARED site
    %% loader instead of answering from the `SEEDED_SITES` constant it was handed. Both
    %% of its readers moved — `getSites`' `publishedPattern` and `siteDraftTest`'s BEFORE
    %% column — so the screen, the live pipeline (`readThroughSitesFor`) and the
    %% Simulator (`evaluateApi`) now all resolve sites through ONE read path and CANNOT
    %% disagree by construction (EXP-047: N-1 readers become projections of the first).
    sitesApi --> loadEffectiveSitePatterns

    %% classDef def065changed marks the ONE node DEF-ROC-065 changed: `sitesApi`.
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: `loadEffectiveSitePatterns` (not one character changed —
    %% it was already the single source of truth and already fail-safe; what changed is
    %% who calls it), `siteDraftTest`/`siteConfig`/`sitePatternStorePort`/`sitePatternStore`
    %% (untouched), and `pipeline`/`evaluateApi` (they were ALREADY on the fold — that is
    %% precisely why the screen was the one disagreeing). `configReadHttp`/`readApi` are
    %% unmarked too: the deployed and local hosts already passed the store AND the
    %% baseline into this seam, so the fix needed no composition change on either root —
    %% which is why one edge closed a defect on both.
    classDef def065changed fill:#e0f7fa,stroke:#00695c,stroke-width:2px;
    class sitesApi def065changed;
    sitesApi --> decisionLogQueryPort

    %% UC-ROC-057 mandatory draft-test path: read-api hosts the draftTestApi seam,
    %% which samples the decision log (recent window), folds the published set +
    %% swaps the draft in, and computes the before/after delta via the SAME engine
    %% the Simulator/pipeline use (draftTest -> evaluateWithTrace, parity/DEF-005).
    %% It mints the content-hash attestation via the store port (attestation
    %% methods ADDED to ruleConfigStorePort this UC).
    draftTest --> evaluateTrace
    %% DEF-ROC-005-class rework (UC-057 live-reject): draftTest imports pipeline's
    %% isFaultStatus/FAULT_STATUS (single source, no copy) to mirror the live
    %% pipeline's isFaultEvent gate — a NON-fault sampled event short-circuits to
    %% the pipeline's recognised/no-alert outcome in BOTH before and after, so
    %% broadening a rule onto a non-fault status never fabricates a before/after alert.
    draftTest --> pipeline

    %% UC-ROC-077 fault-gate generalisation (SLC-ROC-020): ONE predicate module.
    %% faultStatus reads NORMALISE's own emitted vocabulary (ALERT_STATUS_TOKENS)
    %% so the gate cannot drift from what the parser can produce; rules keys its
    %% seeded fault rules on the SAME constant; pipeline imports it for its own
    %% isFaultEvent gate AND re-exports it, so draftTest's existing
    %% `draftTest --> pipeline` parity edge (above) now resolves transitively to
    %% this one definition — no second predicate exists to diverge.
    faultStatus --> normalise
    rules --> faultStatus
    pipeline --> faultStatus
    %% DEF-ROC-015 NEW EDGE: the Simulator's trace engine now imports the SAME gate
    %% DIRECTLY (not via pipeline — that would be a domain cycle through rules). So
    %% BOTH rule-evaluation entry points apply one predicate, and a source pin
    %% (faultStatusGate.test.ts) asserts these two are the ONLY production callers of
    %% the ungated `rulesEngine.decideForSite` — the structural half of the fix.
    evaluateTrace --> faultStatus
    draftTestApi --> draftTest
    draftTestApi --> ruleDraft
    draftTestApi --> canonicalRuleHash
    draftTestApi --> loadEffectiveRules
    draftTestApi --> ruleConfigStorePort
    draftTestApi --> decisionLogQueryPort
    readApi --> draftTestApi

    %% UC-058 publish path: read-api hosts the publishApi seam; publish re-validates
    %% (ruleDraft), recomputes the hash (canonicalRuleHash), runs the by-construction
    %% gate (publishGate) over the attestation read, and appends the version + clears
    %% the draft via the store port. Pipeline + Simulator pick it up via the shared
    %% loader (loadEffectiveCatalogue) with no redeploy (AC-058-3/5).
    publishGate --> canonicalRuleHash
    publishGate --> ruleConfigStorePort
    publishApi --> publishGate
    publishApi --> ruleDraft
    publishApi --> canonicalRuleHash
    publishApi --> ruleConfigStorePort
    readApi --> publishApi
    %% UC-070 template publish EXECUTION: the SAME /api/rules/publish endpoint
    %% dispatches to templatePublishApi when the body carries scope:"template". It
    %% reuses the dual gate (templatePublishGate domain) + the scope-parametric store
    %% appendVersion + the fail-CLOSED link resolver re-read (CC-T7).
    templatePublishApi --> templatePublishGate
    templatePublishApi --> ruleDraft
    templatePublishApi --> canonicalRuleHash
    templatePublishApi --> canonicalLinkedSitesHash
    templatePublishApi --> ruleConfigStorePort
    templatePublishApi --> linkResolver
    readApi --> templatePublishApi
    templatePublishGate --> canonicalRuleHash
    templatePublishGate --> ruleConfigStorePort
    %% UC-058 no-redeploy pickup: the consumer host (host/composition.ts, node
    %% soakPollerHost) wires makeDecide's injected read-through rulesFor from the
    %% config-selected RuleConfig store via the shared loader. pipeline itself holds
    %% NO loader edge — rulesFor is injected (default SEEDED_RULES when absent).
    soakPollerHost --> selectRuleConfigStore
    soakPollerHost --> ruleConfigStore
    soakPollerHost --> loadEffectiveRules
    soakPollerHost --> loadEffectiveSitePatterns
    soakPollerHost --> selectSitePatternStore
    soakPollerHost --> sitePatternStore
    selectRuleConfigStore --> ruleConfigStore

    %% forwarder wiring (pure relay, no domain)
    forwarder --> telPort
    forwarder --> logProdPort

    %% consumer wiring: injected decide + ports
    consumer --> logConsPort
    consumer --> jiraPort
    consumer --> alertStatePort
    consumer --> pipeline
    %% UC-ROC-013: the consumer now folds an identity's log + calls decideRecovery
    %% and builds the recovery comment (direct domain import) — new edge.
    consumer --> decisionRecord

    %% domain composition
    pipeline --> normalise
    pipeline --> decisionRecord
    pipeline --> deviceCode
    %% NEW EDGE (DEF-ROC-039, delta 018 s5.1): decideRules resolves the RAISE input through
    %% the shared guard so its drop can be NAMED; it still reads deviceCode directly for the
    %% rules-engine MATCHING dimension, which must classify and never reject.
    pipeline --> deviceEnumGuard
    pipeline --> siteConfig
    pipeline --> alertPayload
    pipeline --> jiraPort
    pipeline --> rulesEngine
    %% NEW EDGE (DELTA 019, SLC-ROC-026): decideRules computes the hold threshold as
    %% max(eventTs + delay, window_end) through the new pure window module. The ABSENCE of the
    %% sibling edges is load-bearing and pinned: soakExpiry and soakSweep must NOT import it.
    pipeline --> maintenanceWindow
    maintenanceWindow --> actualStart
    %% DELTA 019 / UC-ROC-095 FAULT-4 (EXP-047, one derivation): the ONE shared
    %% offset-tolerant instant parse. `epochMs` existed TWICE (soakExpiry's private copy
    %% and the store adapter's, which DEF-ROC-034 had already delegated to
    %% alertIdentityKey.parseEventTsMs). maintenanceWindow needed a THIRD, which is how a
    %% +HHMM event would be placed in its window LEXICALLY and silently miss it - so both
    %% remaining copies now consume the ONE domain parse, source-pinned by AC-095-6.
    maintenanceWindow --> identityKey
    soakExpiry --> identityKey
    %% DELTA 019 / UC-ROC-095: decisionRecord TYPE-imports the HoldReason union (the
    %% record's holdReason provenance column). `import type`, so the compiler ERASES it and
    %% the emitted JavaScript contains no import at all - and it is NOT the forbidden edge:
    %% soakExpiry and soakSweep still import NOTHING from maintenanceWindow (source-pinned).
    decisionRecord --> maintenanceWindow
    pipeline --> rules
    rules --> rulesEngine
    %% NEW NODE + NEW EDGE (delta 018 s5, DEF-ROC-038 + DEF-ROC-039): the device-enum
    %% guard is DOMAIN-owned and read by BOTH raise paths, so the two cannot invent
    %% divergent guards (the reason these two defects were taken as ONE design). It reads
    %% the ONE dropdown definition rather than re-typing the enum.
    deviceEnumGuard --> deviceCode
    %% TYPE-ONLY EDGE (DEF-ROC-039): DecisionRecord.noAlertReason is the guard's NoAlertReason
    %% union, so a future named drop-reason must be declared there and cannot be an ad-hoc string.
    decisionRecord --> deviceEnumGuard
    decisionRecord --> normalise
    %% DEF-ROC-093 (REWORK) — THREE NEW EDGES OUT OF THE FOLD, and they are worth
    %% pausing on because they are the first time `decisionRecord` reaches a PORT type.
    %% `coverageRaise` rebuilds a PPSM Alert from a STORED fault record when the coverage
    %% reconciliation finds a faulted device with no open ticket. It is the SAME rebuild
    %% `soakExpiry` has done from a stored `held-until` record since UC-ROC-049 — same
    %% `buildCreateAlertInput`, same TOTAL `resolveDeviceEnum` guard, same
    %% `recordedEventAlertStatus` off the stored event column — so these edges make the
    %% third raise-builder use the SAME two decisions as the other two rather than
    %% growing a third opinion (EXP-047). `jiraPort` is reached for the INPUT TYPE only;
    %% the fold performs no I/O and holds no client.
    decisionRecord --> alertPayload
    decisionRecord --> alertStatusField
    decisionRecord -->|"CreateAlertInput type only, no I/O"| jiraPort
    %% DEF-ROC-030: the key-legality decision is DOMAIN-owned and read by three
    %% callers - the consumer lane (validate-then-quarantine, the only lane fed
    %% untrusted payload text), the write adapter (fail-CLOSED inside the key path, so
    %% the control is a property of the PRIMITIVE not an optional courtesy of each
    %% caller - EXP-121) and the read adapter (which must not offer the reserved
    %% quarantine partition as a real NODE). identityKey imports only DecisionRecord's
    %% type, so the domain stays acyclic.
    identityKey --> decisionRecord
    consumer --> identityKey
    %% NEW EDGE (DEF-ROC-039, delta 018 s4/s5.1): the consumer emits the named drop's OWN
    %% signal, worded by the SHARED guard so the immediate and soak paths cannot describe one
    %% fault two different ways, and records the device_code_unmapped tripwire (both limbs).
    consumer --> deviceEnumGuard
    tableStore --> identityKey
    tableStoreQuery --> identityKey
    %% NEW EDGE (delta 017 s5(1), DEF-ROC-030 rework): soakSweep now reads the primitive
    %% DIRECTLY. Widening a validator RETROACTIVELY INVALIDATES rows written under the old
    %% rule, so the sweep's declared inheritance ("its identities were validated on the way
    %% in") is FALSIFIED for a pre-existing blank-identity held-until row: listExpiredHolds
    %% still returns it and queryByIdentity then fails closed. The sweep therefore makes the
    %% check EXPLICITLY and skips such a candidate PERMANENTLY (its own identityRejected
    %% count, never `failed` - which would promise a next-tick retry that can never be kept),
    %% signalled ONCE via the existing store-side claim marker, never a throw.
    soakSweep --> identityKey
    %% NEW EDGE (DEF-ROC-038, delta 018 s5.2): the sweep reads the guard's own signal
    %% fields for the PERMANENT skip it now makes - the second permanent-failure door,
    %% and the one that opens on 19.5% of real traffic. It decides NOTHING itself: the
    %% decision is domain-owned (decideSoakExpiryPermanentSkip) and gated on the SAME
    %% raise gate as decideSoakExpiry, so it fires only for a candidate that would
    %% OTHERWISE HAVE RAISED and can never contradict it.
    soakSweep --> deviceEnumGuard
    %% NEW EDGE (DEF-ROC-049): the sweep asks the domain whether a failed create can
    %% have left a ticket behind. It is a DOMAIN question (an at-most-once invariant),
    %% not an adapter detail, which is why it is not a JiraApiAdapter helper.
    soakSweep --> raiseFailure
    consumer --> raiseFailure
    normalise --> actualStart
    alertPayload --> actualStart
    alertPayload --> jiraPort

    %% UC-ROC-049 soak-expiry raise (pure domain decision): builds the alert from
    %% the held record's original fault data + reuses the device-code normaliser.
    soakExpiry --> alertPayload
    %% EDGE REDIRECTED (DEF-ROC-038, delta 018 s5.2): soakExpiry no longer reads the raw
    %% classifier deviceCode - its `toDeviceCode(held.device) ?? held.device` fallback was
    %% the defect - it now reads the TOTAL deviceEnumGuard, the SAME guard the immediate
    %% path uses, so the two raise paths cannot hold different opinions about what is
    %% nameable in Jira.
    soakExpiry --> deviceEnumGuard
    soakExpiry --> decisionRecord

    %% UC-ROC-078: BOTH raise paths resolve the Jira Alert-Status field through the
    %% ONE decision, which reads NORMALISE's own emitted vocabulary + mapping-table
    %% Unknown row — so the field value cannot drift from what the parser classifies
    %% and the two paths cannot disagree with each other (EXP-047). These three edges
    %% REPLACE the two per-path hardcoded literals (no edge at all, one constant each).
    alertStatusField --> normalise
    soakExpiry --> alertStatusField

    %% DEF-ROC-114 moved the RESOLUTION into the payload builder, so this NEW edge
    %% REPLACES the old `pipeline --> alertStatusField` (removed): the immediate path now
    %% hands on `event.status` UNNARROWED and alertPayload derives BOTH the named fault
    %% and the dropdown value. The two REBUILT paths keep their edge but for the RAW
    %% reader `recordedEventStatus` instead of the narrowing one. Net effect: there is
    %% exactly ONE place a status becomes ticket text, so no call site can narrow early
    %% (which is the bug) or make the summary and the field disagree (EXP-047).
    alertPayload --> alertStatusField
    %% alertStatusField now also reads the ONE fault vocabulary — the same set the
    %% pipeline gate and the seeded rules use — so "what a ticket may name" and "what
    %% may raise a ticket" cannot drift apart.
    alertStatusField --> faultStatus

    %% UC-ROC-049 time-driven sweep: the pass drives the ports; the LOCAL poller
    %% adapter implements the trigger port; PROD swaps in an Azure Timer.
    soakSweep --> alertStatePort
    soakSweep --> jiraPort
    soakSweep --> decisionRecord
    soakSweep --> soakExpiry
    soakSweep --> resolveLease
    intervalSoakTrigger -->|"implements"| soakTriggerPort

    %% UC-ROC-050 soak-poller wiring: the running local host composes the sweep
    %% (store + Jira selection) and drives it behind the trigger port (LOCAL
    %% interval poller). Thin wiring only — no new domain logic.
    soakPollerHost --> soakSweep
    soakPollerHost --> soakTriggerPort
    soakPollerHost --> intervalSoakTrigger
    soakPollerHost --> alertStatePort
    soakPollerHost --> jiraPort

