    %% `jiraTicketHref` — https-only, must end in THIS record's key, no key ⇒ no link).
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: `decisionPage` and `decisionApi`. The table cell is
    %% still dead text. That is RAISED SEPARATELY rather than folded in: it is a
    %% DIFFERENT component (`JiraKeyCell`, `DecisionLogPage.tsx`), not the same one, and
    %% DEF-ROC-105 is live in that file.
    %% `decisionApi` passes the new field through untouched (it types nothing).
    classDef def116changed fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0,stroke-width:2px;
    class jiraTicketUrl,readApi,azureFunctionsHost,decisionView def116changed;

    %% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    %% DEF-ROC-115 — THE QUARANTINE SEAM. A build/gate seam, modelled because it
    %% behaves exactly like a runtime one: two gates held contradictory beliefs
    %% about the SAME path and nothing in the model said they were coupled, so
    %% clearing one necessarily broke the other. cf5ab37 cleared a lint red by
    %% COMMITTING the DEF-ROC-076 artefact, the quarantine assertion went red on
    %% trunk, and deploy-test was SKIPPED for about 12h — the DEF-ROC-086
    %% dark-deploy class — swallowing DEF-ROC-111 value-5 fix.
    quarantineContract["src/contracts/quarantined-paths.json<br/>DEF-ROC-115 THE SINGLE DECLARATION of every path kept ON DISK as evidence and NEVER committed, plus the ENUMERATED set of tools that walk the disk. Today one entry: src/app/local/probe-real-bus-send.ts, the DEF-ROC-076 artefact whose unmarked sends Service Bus ACKS and discards. DATA, never imported by any runtime, same posture as roc-test-marker.json and simulator-publish-body.json. THE INVARIANT IT EXISTS TO STATE: a path that may never be committed must not be inside ANY on-disk scanner scope, because such a scanner red can only be cleared by editing the file and an edit nobody may commit is not a fix"]:::def115changed
    quarantineGate["src/app/tests/unit/def115QuarantineJointSatisfiability + tests/unit/_quarantineScope<br/>DEF-ROC-115 the JOINT-SATISFIABILITY gate, exposed as make quarantine-gate. THE QUESTION IS ABOUT CONFIGURATION NOT THE FILESYSTEM - would this scanner READ this path IF it were on disk. That correction is the whole of 28a8b9bd: the artefact is UNTRACKED so it exists only in the checkout that made it, and the first cut asked whether it was in the scanner PROGRAM, a question about the disk, which answered green locally and RED on CI with a false evidence-missing violation and a non-vacuity arm that could not fail - it turned trunk red and SKIPPED the deploy, the very class this gate exists to prevent. ABSENCE FROM DISK MEANS THE QUARANTINE HELD and is never a violation. Split in two ON PURPOSE: auditQuarantine is PURE and consults no filesystem at all so it can be pointed at a CONTRADICTORY tree and shown red, and the resolvers are REAL - ESLint.isPathIgnored, pure pattern matching and measured existence-independent, and ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent over a CONSTRUCTED SHADOW TREE that materialises the path and carries every real tsconfig at its real relative position so extends and references resolve as they do for real. Never a second copy of the ignore list and never a hand-rolled include/exclude reimplementation. FIVE cases CONSTRUCT the contradiction and EVERY ONE runs in CI: a synthetic admitting config, a synthetic committed quarantine, cf5ab37 eslint config rebuilt as a delta from today, a proof the tsc resolver CAN say in-scope on an unexcluded path, and the tsconfig rebuilt without its exclude - each measured RED under mutation in the ARTEFACT-ABSENT world. It also SWEEPS every tracked eslint.config and tsconfig and fails on one that is not declared, so a NEW scanner cannot appear without stating what it does about the quarantine"]:::def115changed
    appLintConfig["src/app/eslint.config.js + src/tools/replay-injector/eslint.config.js<br/>DEF-ROC-115 REDIRECTED: both flat configs now BUILD their ignores by READING quarantined-paths.json rather than restating a path. The injector has nothing quarantined today and is wired anyway, so the day something is, its lint gate excludes it automatically instead of going red for everyone on a file nobody may commit. src/app config carried the incident: before it ignored the artefact, lint scanned it on disk and FOUR separate agents each paid to report the same red as not-theirs"]:::def115changed
    appTsconfig["src/app/tsconfig.json<br/>DEF-ROC-115 THE SECOND INSTANCE, found BY the gate rather than by an outage: include is src local tests, so make typecheck was type-checking the quarantined artefact off disk. It happened to be type-clean, so nobody noticed - a dependency bump would have turned the shared type-check red with the same single escape, the commit that trips the quarantine. A tsconfig cannot READ json at load time, so it RESTATES the path in exclude and the gate re-derives its real file set with the compiler own include/exclude expansion. Restate-and-pin, exactly as roc-test-marker.json four copies are pinned"]:::def115changed
    sbLaneCoverageGate["src/tools/replay-injector/tests/serviceBusLaneCoverage<br/>DEF-ROC-076 AC-076-3 lane-coverage gate, REDIRECTED by DEF-ROC-115: its quarantined lane rows are now READ from quarantined-paths.json and it asserts the path literal appears NOWHERE in its own source, so the quarantine list and the scanner exclusions cannot fork again. This gate asserts a fact about ANOTHER package tracking, which is why it could contradict src/app lint config in the first place"]:::def115changed

    appLintConfig -->|"reads the single declaration"| quarantineContract
    sbLaneCoverageGate -->|"reads the single declaration"| quarantineContract
    quarantineGate --> quarantineContract
    quarantineGate -->|"resolves scope via ESLint isPathIgnored"| appLintConfig
    quarantineGate -->|"resolves scope via ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent"| appTsconfig
    sbLaneCoverageGate -->|"declares every committed publish lane, incl. this one"| replaySb

    %% classDef def115changed marks the nodes DEF-ROC-115 added and redirected —
    %% the single quarantine declaration, the joint-satisfiability gate, the two
    %% flat configs that now READ it, the tsconfig that restates it under the
    %% gate, and the DEF-ROC-076 lane gate that no longer holds its own copy.
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: appRocTestMarker, sbPublisher and every runtime
    %% publish node. No runtime behaviour changed here at all — what changed is
    %% which files a build gate reads, and whether two gates can disagree.
    classDef def115changed fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#6a1b9a,stroke-width:2px;
    class quarantineContract,quarantineGate,appLintConfig,appTsconfig,sbLaneCoverageGate def115changed;

    %% ── DEF-ROC-085 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    %% classDef def085changed marks what DEF-ROC-085 changed: `tableStore`'s append,
    %% and the NEW `structuredLog` node the store now depends on.
    %%
    %% REPRODUCED FIRST, against real Azurite, because the item's evidence was a CODE
    %% READING and this project has had that class disproved twice (DEF-ROC-053,
    %% DEF-ROC-081). Two DISTINCT decision records sharing node/device/eventTs/messageId
    %% were appended: the second `append` threw NOTHING, `queryByIdentity` returned ONE
    %% record, and a raw partition listing held exactly one physical row
    %% (`0639233352001230000|0`). The second event's outcome and payload were gone with
    %% no error, no line and no counter - the DEF-ROC-022 shape.
    %%
    %% BEHAVIOUR CHANGED (`tableStore`): a 409 used to be UNCONDITIONALLY a redelivery
    %% no-op. It is now READ BACK and the stored EVENT compared. Same event means a
    %% genuine redelivery, byte-for-byte the old behaviour (a redelivery recomputes
    %% recordedTs and may re-decide the OUTCOME - the DEF-ROC-104 lost-lease `cleared` -
    %% and neither makes it a new event). A DIFFERENT event is a COLLISION: the record is
    %% RESCUED under `{eventTicks:D19}|{messageId}|c{n}`, NAMED on one queryable
    %% `DecisionRowKeyCollision` line, and STAMPED (`rowKeyCollision`,
    %% `collidedWithRowKey`) so the drop that did not happen is countable in the STORE and
    %% not only in a trace that ages out. Exhaustion RAISES
    %% `DecisionRowKeyCollisionUnresolvedError`; a read-back that FAILS is PROPAGATED,
    %% never swallowed as a redelivery.
    %%
    %% WHY THE SUFFIX IS LEGITIMATE NOW: delta 017 Ruling 2 forbade any POSITIONAL split
    %% of this RowKey until the calendar bound existed; DEF-ROC-034 delivered it, so the
    %% ticks prefix is guaranteed 19 digits and DIGITS ONLY.
    %%
    %% GRAPH-CHANGED: NEW node `structuredLog` with edges from all SEVEN of its real
    %% importers. Only `tableStore` is new CODE; the other six are the routing path that
    %% was already there and unmarked - the same finding DEF-ROC-112 recorded about
    %% `hostInvocation`, and exactly the seam a change-impact model exists to expose.
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: `consumer`, `hostInvocation`, `identityKey`,
    %% `decisionRecord`, `tableStoreQuery`. None of their behaviour changed. The two new
    %% columns are additive and non-load-bearing (schemaVersion stays 0), and nothing
    %% parses a messageId back out of a RowKey, so no read is affected.
    structuredLog["src/telemetry/structuredLog<br/>DEF-ROC-041 the ONE place a structured signal becomes a line the SINK can be QUERIED by: structuredLine(level,event,fields) emits a SINGLE JSON argument because App Insights stores a console.* line as one util.format STRING that KQL parse_json refuses; event+level are FIELDS a caller cannot shadow; never throws (a logging call sits on the failure path of a consumer whose posture is record-and-checkpoint); an Error is DESCRIBED because JSON.stringify(Error) is {}. LOG_JOIN_KEY names the documented quarantineMessageId hop once, for the emitter, the runbook and make query-rejected-identity alike. Modelled by DEF-ROC-085: it was imported by seven modules and drawn by none"]
    sbPublisher --> structuredLog
    sbSource --> structuredLog
    consumer --> structuredLog
    hostInvocation --> structuredLog
    simPublishForHost --> structuredLog
    simCapForHost --> structuredLog
    tableStore -->|"DEF-ROC-085 DecisionRowKeyCollision"| structuredLog
    classDef def085changed fill:#ede7f6,stroke:#5e35b1,stroke-width:2px;
    class tableStore,structuredLog def085changed;

    %% ── DEF-ROC-121 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    %% classDef def121changed marks the ONE node DEF-ROC-121 changed: `decisionPage`.
    %% DEF-ROC-116 made the DRAWER's Jira key a link and deliberately left the TABLE
    %% cell alone (a different component, in a file DEF-ROC-105 was live in). The
    %% table is the surface a responder SCANS FIRST, so the dead text stayed exactly
    %% where the cost is paid: measured live on buildSha 80e6908 by this item's own
    %% committed spec, ZERO anchors in the table for a keyed row while ROC-27's
    %% drawer entry resolved to a real ticket.
    %%
    %% NO NEW EDGE, and that is the point: `decisionPage --> decisionView` already
    %% existed, and the fix REUSES `jiraTicketHref` across it rather than deriving a
    %% second answer to "is this url safe". Two surfaces, one refusal rule (https
    %% only, must end in THIS record's key, no key => no link whatever was served),
    %% so they cannot drift apart.
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: `decisionView`, `readApi`, `azureFunctionsHost`,
    %% `jiraTicketUrl`, `decisionApi`. Not one line of them changed — DEF-ROC-116
    %% already served `jiraUrl` on every record INCLUDING the ones the table renders,
    %% which is exactly why this item was cheap. `C_TABLE` in component-map is not
    %% marked either: the house table component is untouched; what changed is what
    %% one cell puts INSIDE it.
    classDef def121changed fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px;
    class decisionPage def121changed;

    %% ── DEF-ROC-118 — the Simulator's CLOSED state gains a SIGNPOST (never a control) ──
    %% classDef def118changed marks the ONE node DEF-ROC-118 changed: `simulatorPage`.
    %% In the ESTABLISHED-closed state ONLY, it now renders a second region below the
    %% strip carrying the FIRST ANCHORS this page has ever had. Owner-reported and
    %% reproduced live on buildSha 4eb6651: the whole page had ZERO anchors, no command
    %% and no named owner, and the message named an environment variable and then said
    %% the route stays inert until "an operator deliberately opens a window" - said to
    %% the person who IS the operator. The capability was delivered, validated (real
    %% tickets ROC-26/ROC-27) and UNREACHABLE BY ITS OWN USERS.
    %%
    %% THE NEW EDGE IS OUTWARD AND IS NOT CODE: the page now depends on TWO DOCUMENTS by
    %% URL - docs/runbooks/simulator-live-publish.md s2 and docs/SIMULATOR-PROOF.md s4
    %% step 1. `make check-docs` scans markdown and CANNOT see a link living in TSX, so
    %% each #fragment is pinned against a real heading in the target file by
    %% SimulatorPage.def118.test.tsx (AC-118-2). Without that pin this edge rots silently.
    %%
    %% WHY A SIGN AND NOT A BUTTON, which is a GRAPH fact rather than a preference:
    %% `publishRoute` is authLevel ANONYMOUS BY FORCE (delta 020 DECISION 2) and this
    %% dashboard is served with no sign-in, so a control here would be a control for the
    %% whole internet, arming a real write that raises real Jira tickets. AC-118-4 pins
    %% that PREMISE at source - the write route's authLevel, AND the `easyAuthPrincipal`
    %% seam being consumed by NOTHING - so the day REQ-ROC-005 lands the pin turns RED
    %% and the decision is genuinely reopened rather than quietly inherited.
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: `publishCapabilityDomain` and `publishApiClient` - the
    %% signpost reads no new fact and makes no new call, it renders on a state those
    %% modules already derive. `simPublishHttp` likewise: this change adds NO path to the
    %% write route, and AC-118-4 asserts ZERO non-GET requests in the closed state.
    classDef def118changed fill:#fffde7,stroke:#f57f17,stroke-width:2px;
    class simulatorPage def118changed;


    %% ── UC-ROC-107's WINDOW SUBGRAPH IS DELETED (UC-ROC-117) ──────────────────────
    %% It modelled `simulator/window`'s HTTP adapter, its seam, its composition root, the
    %% window store port and the Table Storage adapter behind it. DEF-ROC-123 deleted all
    %% five FILES and this graph was never brought with them — five nodes and fifteen edges
    %% describing modules that had not existed on disk for days, which is precisely the
    %% false signal `make impacted-tests` reads off this file.
    %%
    %% UC-ROC-117 removes the last node they hung from (`simPublishWindow`), so the block is
    %% removed rather than left half-unmoored. What it recorded is worth one sentence: the
    %% window moved from an app setting into a store row so an operator could open one from
    %% the screen with no `az` call and no 30-60s restart. The reason that whole design is
    %% gone is that the App Service access gate is now live and the window was a time-box
    %% standing in for an auth control that did not exist yet.

    %% ── UC-ROC-105 (SLC-ROC-029, after UC-ROC-104) — the Simulator's hold LABEL ─────
    %% THE NODE THAT WAS MISSING. The browser's Simulator view-model has carried the
    %% hold WORDING since UC-ROC-035 and was never modelled — only `simulatorPage` was —
    %% so `@covers simulatorViewModel` (on simulator.test.ts since UC-ROC-035) resolved to
    %% nothing and a behaviour change in the derivations was structurally unable to show up
    %% as an IMPACTED node. Modelled now, on the ACTUAL routing path: the page calls these
    %% pure derivations and renders their return verbatim.
    simulatorViewModel["dashboard/domain/simulator<br/>UC-105 the browser's pure derivations over the /api/evaluate body (heldDetailLine, outcomeBanner, traceEmptyLine, siteResolutionLine, toEvaluateRequest) plus the DTO MIRROR of the app domain's EvaluationTrace - re-declared, never imported, so the bundle stays free of the Node/@azure adapters, and BOUND to the app source by pins that resolve the expectation FROM it (STATUS_VALUES, EvaluationOutcome and now HoldReason). BEHAVIOUR CHANGED: heldDetailLine rendered 'Held for {delay}s before it would raise (soak window)' for EVERY held-until outcome, so once UC-ROC-104 generalised the deadline to max(event+delay, window_end) the sentence stated the WRONG WAIT and the WRONG MECHANISM for a window-extended hold - the screen contradicting its own returned data, on the one surface P1/P2 consult to find out why an alert did not raise. NOW BRANCHED ON THE REASON, never on whether a window is recorded: a covering window the delay OUTLASTED is holdReason soak and keeps the delivered wording byte-for-byte (UC-104 AC-104-2 - one assignment rule, not two), and only maintenance-window gets the new sentence naming the window and its end. THE DEADLINE IS result.heldUntil IN BOTH BRANCHES and is NEVER re-derived from delay or holdWindowEnd (EXP-047: a second computation of one value is the drift class this project has already paid for); holdWindowEnd is rendered only as the WINDOW's own end, a different fact that merely coincides with the deadline in every response the real producer can emit. Its pins compare INSTANTS, parsed, not strings - deliberately NOT the localeCompare collation DEF-ROC-071 records on the app's absorb boundary"]:::uc105changed

    %% ── edges ──
    %% Already the runtime path since UC-ROC-035 and only now drawn: SimulatorPage calls
    %% heldDetailLine/outcomeBanner/traceEmptyLine/siteResolutionLine and renders each
    %% return verbatim, so a wording change in the view-model IS a screen change.
    simulatorPage --> simulatorViewModel

    %% classDef uc105changed marks what UC-ROC-105 changed.
    %%
    %% ADDED: simulatorViewModel (the node, not the module — the module has existed since
    %% UC-ROC-035; what was missing was its presence in this graph).
    %%
    %% BEHAVIOUR-CHANGED:
    %%   simulatorViewModel - heldDetailLine now branches on `holdReason`, and the DTO
    %%                        mirror gains holdReason/holdWindowId/holdWindowEnd plus a
    %%                        HoldReason union pinned to the app domain's own.
    %%   simulatorPage      - the TEXT under `sim-held-detail` changes for a window-
    %%                        extended hold. No new element, no new class, no colour cue:
    %%                        the distinction is carried by words (AC-105-4 / WCAG 1.4.1),
    %%                        and the page's own JSX is unchanged — which is itself the
    %%                        finding, so it is marked for its RENDERED behaviour, not for
    %%                        a diff a tester could read.
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: evaluateTrace / maintenanceWindow / evaluateApi. UC-ROC-104
    %% already produces every field this UC reads; nothing app-side changed, and marking any
    %% of them would send a tester looking for a server change that does not exist.
    classDef uc105changed fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#e65100,stroke-width:2px;
    class simulatorPage,simulatorViewModel uc105changed;

    %% ================= UC-ROC-093 — the trainer/trainee practice cycle =================
    %% @alias replayPracticeDeps=replay-injector.localPractice
    %% @alias replayPracticeAudit=replay-injector.practiceAudit
    %% @alias replayLocalMain=replay-injector.localMain
    %% @alias uc093PracticeCycle=acceptance.uc093PracticeCycle
    %% Two aliases for PRE-EXISTING nodes, added here because UC-ROC-093's new edges make
    %% them impacted and `make impacted-tests` could not name a covering spec for either —
    %% an alias gap, not a coverage gap: `publishBoundary.test.ts` and `parse.test.ts` have
    %% covered them since UC-ROC-027/031. A node the tool cannot resolve reports as
    %% UNCOVERED and sends a tester looking for work that is already done.
    %% @alias replaySb=replay-injector.publish
    %% @alias replayXlsx=replay-injector.parse
    replayPracticeDeps["replay-injector practice/localPractice UC-093 NEW<br/>the LOCAL PRACTICE COMPOSITION ROOT — a SECOND composition beside main.ts productionDeps, not a second allowlist entry: widening ALLOWED_NAMESPACES would have made every practice run able to reach the cloud too, which is the opposite of the UC's own done condition. Owns its OWN committed closed allowlist LOCAL_ALLOWED_NAMESPACES holding exactly the emulator host localhost, so DURING A PRACTICE RUN the cloud aas-test namespace is refused as firmly as a production one (same assertNamespaceAllowed guard, same exact match, an empty list would still refuse everything). THREE INDEPENDENT REASONS a practice run cannot reach a cloud bus: (1) the GUARD runs first and aborts before any auth/parse/publish/network; (2) the AUTH resolves the emulator connection string and NOTHING else — this lane imports no @azure/identity and no @azure/keyvault-secrets so there is no code path to a real credential, and an operator-supplied ROC_SERVICEBUS_CONNECTION_STRING naming a servicebus.windows.net host is REFUSED fail-closed via EmulatorConnectionRequiredError; (3) the emulator connection string's own endpoint is the localhost AMQP listener. Wraps resolveAuth+createSender with the audit sink — the two stages run() reaches ONLY AFTER the guard passes, which is what makes the trail evidence about the guard's verdict"]:::uc093changed
    replayPracticeAudit["replay-injector practice/practiceAudit UC-093 NEW<br/>JSONL stage-crossing trail at ROC_PRACTICE_AUDIT: auth_resolved / sender_created / published. Exists because AC-093-3 has to establish an ABSENCE and an absence read off stdout is the weakest possible evidence (cf DEF-ROC-125 loop-gate reporting clean at load 56, DEF-ROC-126 board-sweep reporting nothing outstanding over 190 stale items). DELIBERATELY CARRIES NO TIMESTAMPS: the pace a trainee observes must be read off the decision-log surface, never off the injector's own account of itself, and a send time here would be an invitation to do exactly that"]:::uc093changed
    replayLocalMain["replay-injector localMain.ts UC-093 NEW<br/>the trainer's entry point `npm run local:practice -- localhost <workbook> --scenario <name> --pace <ms>`: same runCli, same argument parsing, same guard->auth->parse->publish order as main.ts; only the composition differs and it differs in the direction of safety"]:::uc093changed
    uc093PracticeCycle["tests/acceptance/uc093-practice-cycle UC-093 NEW<br/>the LOCAL end-to-end proof of SLC-ROC-025 measure 4, the role uc006 plays for C1 and uc080 for the status scenarios. Drives the trainer's REAL COMMAND as a CHILD PROCESS (not an in-process re-composition: src/app and the injector are separate npm packages and a cross-package import is a hard TS6059) and reads every observation BACK OFF the decision log. Its warm-up gate is STRONGER than uc006's for a MEASURED reason: uc006 waits for ONE row, which proves ONE of four Event Hubs partitions is claimed, and the first run of this spec read cycle one back as PAPER OUT/ONLINE/MEDIA-OUT/MEDIA-OK — out of publish order — while cycle one and two disagreed; it now waits for EIGHT distinct non-fault rows so round-robin proves every partition is claimed and draining. Emits its read-back via process.stderr.write, NOT console.log, because vitest 4 suppresses console output from a PASSING test and the first version of the tester surface therefore printed nothing at all on green"]:::uc093changed
    replayLocalMain --> replayRun
    replayLocalMain --> replayPracticeDeps
    replayLocalMain --> replayPracticeAudit
    replayPracticeDeps --> replayPracticeAudit
    replayPracticeDeps --> replayXlsx
    replayPracticeDeps --> replaySb
    replayPracticeDeps --> replaySenderPort
    uc093PracticeCycle -. "spawns the trainer command" .-> replayLocalMain
    uc093PracticeCycle --> forwarder
    uc093PracticeCycle --> consumer
    uc093PracticeCycle --> pipeline
    uc093PracticeCycle --> sbSource
    uc093PracticeCycle --> ehProducer
    uc093PracticeCycle --> ehConsumer
    uc093PracticeCycle --> tableStore

    %% classDef uc093changed marks what UC-ROC-093 ADDED. The guard itself
    %% (replayGuard) and the cloud allowlist (replayAllowlist) are NOT marked and that is
    %% deliberate: neither changed by one character. UC-ROC-093 EXERCISES the UC-ROC-029
    %% guard as a live precondition against a SECOND, separately-committed allowlist —
    %% which is the whole point of AC-093-3 — so a tester sent looking for a change in the
    %% guard would find none and rightly distrust the mark. replayRun/replayPace/
    %% replaySenderPort/replaySb are unmarked for the same reason: the practice lane reuses
    %% them verbatim.
    classDef uc093changed fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#0277bd,stroke-width:2px;

    %% =====================================================================
    %% DELTA 021 (CHK-ROC-017 / UC-ROC-112,113,114) — the cross-view filter
    %% carry seam, and SEVEN nodes that were MISSING FROM THE MODEL ENTIRELY.
    %% =====================================================================
    %% FOUND AT THIS GATE AND WORTH MORE THAN THE SEAM ITSELF: the app SHELL and
    %% the whole OVERVIEW surface were UNMODELLED. `App.tsx` (UC-ROC-034),
    %% `AppNav.tsx` (034/040/056/110), `OverviewContainer`/`OverviewPage` (040),
    %% `StatTiles` (041/045) and `domain/overview` (039) have existed for dozens of
    %% use-cases and appear NOWHERE in this graph — grep for `overviewPage` before
    %% this block returns nothing. `App.tsx` is the SOLE OWNER of `view` state and
    %% one of the six sources `captures.json` pins, and a change to it had no node
    %% to mark. That is the DEF-ROC-112 finding again (`hostInvocation`: a module
    %% owning half the record identity, drawn by nobody) applied to the browser:
    %% the file every view switch passes through was invisible to
    %% `make impacted-tests`. They are added here as NEWLY-MODELLED, and the
    %% classDef below marks ONLY what delta 021 actually changes — a reader sent
    %% looking for a change in `appNav` or `overviewStats` would find none.

    %% @alias appShell=dashboard-App,appShell
    %% @alias appNav=dashboard-components-AppNav,appNav
    %% @alias viewIntent=dashboard-domain-viewIntent,viewIntent
    %% @alias decisionContainer=dashboard-components-DecisionLogContainer,decisionContainer
    %% @alias overviewContainer=dashboard-components-OverviewContainer,overviewContainer
    %% @alias overviewPage=dashboard-components-OverviewPage,overviewPage
    %% @alias statTiles=dashboard-components-StatTiles,statTiles
    %% @alias overviewStats=dashboard-domain-overview,overviewStats

    appShell["dashboard/App<br/>UC-ROC-034 the app SHELL and SOLE OWNER of view state: a hand-rolled switcher, NO router (no react-router/useNavigate anywhere in src/dashboard - grep-confirmed 2026-08-27), mounting EXACTLY ONE view so there is always one main and one h1; unmount/remount per switch is what makes the v83 stale-state guard STRUCTURAL. UC-ROC-109 seeds 'overview'. DELTA 021 as BUILT (UC-ROC-112): the view:AppView slot BECOMES nav:ViewIntent - REPLACED, not a second slot beside it - plus ONE navigate() callback; AppNav's onSelect is adapted to navigate({view}) so there is exactly ONE way to change view. A SECOND slot was the delta's first wording and is the bug: an intent cleared in the same transition that sets view is already gone on the render that MOUNTS the destination, so the seed never arrives (FAULT-1). With one slot there is nothing to clear and consumption is structural. A DEPICTED SOURCE in docs/evidence/simulator/captures.json - editing it costs a re-capture at the next DEPLOY, which drives a real PPSM publish and a real Jira ticket"]
    appNav["dashboard/components/AppNav<br/>UC-ROC-034/040/056/110 the Primary nav landmark: 4 ACButton view-switch controls (Overview, Decision Log, Simulator, Config), active marked by aria-current=page AND a filled-vs-outline shape cue never hue alone. NOT a router - it only emits the chosen view upward. DELTA 021: DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED - its onSelect(view) contract is kept and App adapts it, because this is the file DEF-ROC-135 measured as the live rot mismatch. A DEPICTED SOURCE"]
    viewIntent["dashboard/domain/viewIntent<br/>DELTA 021 NEW, PURE, no React: ViewIntent = {view, filter?} - the ONE-SHOT channel a source view uses to hand the destination a preset filter across a view switch. CONSUMED BY THE MOUNTING RENDER, never HELD: because the shell remounts views on every switch, a held value would re-apply a filter the user had cleared (FAULT-2), and a value cleared at hand-off would never arrive at all (FAULT-1). ONE slot closes both - toIntent(view) produces a FILTERLESS intent, so a nav arrival is unseeded by construction. Deliberately shaped like a router's navigate(path,{state}) so the later react-router reversal is a substitution of THIS MODULE, not a rework of every call site - Option 1 and Option 2 are SEQUENCED, not chosen between"]
    decisionContainer["dashboard/components/DecisionLogContainer<br/>UC-ROC-009/010 owns the Decision Log filter state and re-queries the REAL server-side port via useDecisions - NO client-side array filtering. Site dropdown options are METADATA accumulated as a union from the UNFILTERED base load; the rendered ROWS always come from the port. DELTA 021: gains ONE optional prop initialFilter, applied by a LAZY useState initialiser (NOT an effect) so the seed lands on the SAME render that mounts and there is no window in which the destination renders unfiltered (FAULT-1). A DEPICTED SOURCE"]
    overviewContainer["dashboard/components/OverviewContainer<br/>UC-ROC-040 wiring only, no wrapper element: calls the EXISTING useDecisions with a FIXED 24h window - the same /api/decisions?since request the Decision Log issues, no new hook/port/endpoint - and renders the pure OverviewPage as a function of load state. DELTA 021: gains an onNavigate prop threaded to OverviewPage. NOT a depicted source"]
    overviewPage["dashboard/components/OverviewPage<br/>UC-ROC-040 PURE function of the load state - records exist ONLY inside the ready variant, so the stale-prior-state guard is structural and there is no zero-flash. ONE main, ONE h1 'Overview', constant shell + aria-live announce, swapping body. DELTA 021: threads onNavigate to StatTiles and (for UC-113/114) hosts the new breakdown section - the co-owned-file concern SLC-ROC-035 already flagged between UC-113 and UC-114. NOT a depicted source"]
    statTiles["dashboard/components/StatTiles<br/>UC-ROC-041/045 four single-figure count tiles over the loaded window, computed by overviewStats and NEVER re-derived here; non-colour status (text+glyph+weight, ACBadge only reinforces); mounted ONLY inside the ready body. DELTA 021: the THREE outcome tiles become activatable, each emitting {view:'decisions', filter:{outcome:<its token>}}. The fallbackOnly tile is DELIBERATELY NOT linked (AC-112-4: no coverage filter dimension exists to link to). NOT a depicted source"]
    overviewStats["dashboard/domain/overview<br/>UC-ROC-039 PURE overviewStats: the count-by-outcome/coverage derivations the tiles render. DELTA 021: UNCHANGED by the seam; UC-113/114's breakdown group-bys are its natural home, and AC-113-4 FORCES them to be derived from the SAME already-fetched record set the tiles use - a second fetch would be a second derivation of one fact (EXP-047)"]

    %% The seam, as edges. `appShell --> viewIntent` is the whole mechanism: one
    %% typed one-shot value, produced by a source view, consumed by the shell,
    %% seeded into the destination.
    appShell --> appNav
    appShell --> viewIntent
    appShell --> decisionContainer
    appShell --> overviewContainer
    appShell --> simulatorPage
    decisionContainer --> useDecisions
    decisionContainer --> decisionPage
    decisionContainer --> decisionView
    overviewContainer --> useDecisions
    overviewContainer --> overviewPage
    overviewPage --> statTiles
    overviewPage --> decisionView
    statTiles --> overviewStats
    statTiles --> decisionView
    overviewStats --> decisionView
    statTiles -. "DELTA 021: emits a ViewIntent upward" .-> viewIntent
    overviewPage -. "DELTA 021: threads onNavigate" .-> viewIntent
    decisionContainer -. "DELTA 021: seeded by intent.filter" .-> viewIntent

    %% classDef delta021changed marks what DELTA 021 CHANGES. Kept apart from the
    %% newly-modelled-but-unchanged nodes on purpose (the DEF-ROC-098 discipline:
    %% a mark that is wider than the change makes every mark less trustworthy).
    %%
    %% CHANGED BY DELTA 021: viewIntent (new module), appShell (+1 state slot, +1
    %% callback), decisionContainer (+1 seed prop), overviewContainer/overviewPage/
    %% statTiles (+the onNavigate chain and three activatable tiles), and — LANDED
    %% BY UC-ROC-112, not UC-113/114, per delta 021 §1.5's one-re-capture landing
    %% sequence — decisionToolbar (+the DATA-DRIVEN active-dimension handling
    %% FAULT-4 requires) and decisionView (+FILTER_DIMENSIONS/activeFilterDimensions,
    %% with isFilterActive derived from them instead of hand-enumerating
    %% outcome/site/since, so a new dimension cannot be wired into the port call
    %% and forgotten in the toolbar and in Clear). Then — for UC-113/114 only —
    %% decisionView again (+device/status in DecisionFilter and the option
    %% models), decisionApi (+2 params in
    %% buildDecisionsUrl and filterKey), decisionLogQueryPort
    %% (+device/+status on DecisionLogFilter), tableStoreQuery (+a device odata
    %% clause, +a status predicate, +the DERIVED alertStatus field), readApiFilter
    %% AND azureFunctionsHost (BOTH query-string parsers — the DEF-ROC-075 shape:
    %% two hand-kept enumerations of one contract, with nothing red if only one is
    %% changed, which is why delta 021 §3.4 requires a two-root parity pin), and
    %% decisionRecord (+the optional derived alertStatus).
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: appNav (kept byte-identical on purpose — see its
    %% node), overviewStats (the seam does not touch it), tableStore/consumer/
    %% pipeline/foldAlertState (NO write-side change: alertStatus is DERIVED at the
    %% read boundary from eventJson, never a new stored column — a stored column
    %% could only be written going forward, so the breakdown would count from the
    %% blob over ALL rows while the filter matched only NEW rows, disagreeing
    %% permanently for every historic row and requiring a prod-DATA backfill),
    %% webProxy (untouched — this delta is NOT deploy-topology-bearing; that
    %% changes only if the history-API router reversal is taken, which is why
    %% delta 021 §1.2 records hash routing as the cheaper first form).
    classDef delta021changed fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#0277bd,stroke-width:2px;
    class viewIntent,appShell,decisionContainer,overviewContainer,overviewPage,statTiles,decisionToolbar,decisionView delta021changed;

    %% ── DEF-ROC-055 — the SHAPE arm of `created` was an uncaught poison loop ─────
    %% classDef def055changed marks ONLY what this defect changes. Reproduced on the
    %% real consumer path before any fix: `Error: actualStart: unparseable Created
    %% timestamp "yesterday"` thrown from `parts` -> `toActualStartUtc` -> `normalise`
    %% -> `decide` -> `handleEvent`, with NO try/catch on the stack, so the Event Hubs
    %% checkpoint never advanced and the event was never recorded.
    %%
    %% CHANGED: actualStart (both renderers TOTAL — an unparseable `created` is carried
    %% through verbatim instead of thrown), pipeline (the NEW instant gate, one call,
    %% before every reader of the instant), identityKey (its predicate is now the
    %% pipeline's gate too, and `eventTs` joins the escaped/bounded log fields).
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: normalise (unchanged — it still just calls the
    %% renderer), consumer (unchanged — DEF-ROC-034's quarantine gate already handled
    %% this reason; the defect was that nothing could REACH it), maintenanceWindow
    %% (unchanged and still THROWING on purpose — `eventClock`/`effectiveHoldUntil` are
    %% arithmetic AFTER the gate, so a throw there is a programming error and must stay
    %% loud, EXP-121), host/invocation and host/register (no catch was added, on
    %% purpose: a catch there cannot distinguish a permanent bad field from a transient
    %% dependency failure and would swallow the retryable ones).
    classDef def055changed fill:#ffe0e6,stroke:#b02a4a,stroke-width:2px;

    %% classDef def144changed marks ONLY what DEF-ROC-144 changes: the consumer's
    %% unrecognised-type branch and the refusal classifier it now consults. The defect is
    %% a FIFTH instance of the family DEF-ROC-022/030/034/055 close (an event that reached
    %% the consumer left no record) on the ONE path none of their sweeps covered, and the
    %% live measurement corrects the family's shared assumption: on this Event Hubs
    %% trigger a throw is NOT a redelivery, it is a checkpointed silent drop that also
    %% abandons the rest of the batch. TWO SIBLING SITES OF THE SAME CLASS ARE STILL OPEN
    %% and are deliberately NOT marked here because they are NOT changed: the fault raise
    %% (`jira.createAlert`) and the clearing leg's `jira.resolveAlert`, both of which also
    %% throw before the triggering event's record is appended. They are enumerated, with
    %% the reason each needs a different cure, by the AC-144.4 sweep gate in
    %% tests/unit/def144NewTypeTicketRecordLoss.test.ts — a source-level ledger, because
    %% DEF-ROC-049's sweep predicate looked for CLAIM-then-act sites and is structurally
    %% blind to five of the consumer's six Jira egresses.
    classDef def144changed fill:#ffe0e6,stroke:#b02a4a,stroke-width:2px;
    class actualStart,pipeline,identityKey def055changed;

    %% ── UC-ROC-113 — the DEVICE breakdown dimension, and the two parsers ─────────
    %% Delta 021 RULING 2 §2.3. `device` is a new SERVER-SIDE `DecisionLogFilter`
    %% dimension mirroring `site` exactly: a STORED, REQUIRED column (one of the six
    %% in DECISION_ROW_STRING_COLUMNS, present on 42/42 live records), so no
    %% write-side change, no new column, no backfill, no historic cliff.
    %%
    %% THE NEW NODE IS THE POINT, and it is not the dimension. `decisionFilterQuery`
    %% is ONE registry + ONE parser that BOTH composition roots now call. Before it,
    %% `local/readApiFilter` and `azureFunctionsHost` each hand-marshalled the
    %% dimension list with NOTHING red if only one was changed (P0.9, the DEF-ROC-075
    %% shape) — and UC-113, being the first UC to ADD a dimension, is exactly where
    %% that bites: `device` wired into the local root alone is green in every unit,
    %% browser and local end-to-end test while the DEPLOYED host ignores the parameter
    %% and serves an UNNARROWED list under a breakdown row claiming N. So AC-DIM-1's
    %% parity is now BY CONSTRUCTION (EXP-047: one writer, not two enumerations held
    %% together by a pin), and the registry is typed `Record<keyof DecisionLogFilter,…>`
    %% so a key added to the port and not registered is a COMPILE error.
    %% @alias decisionFilterQuery=domain-decisionFilterQuery,decisionFilterQuery
    decisionFilterQuery["src/domain/decisionFilterQuery<br/>UC-ROC-113 NEW, PURE, cloud-agnostic: the ONE declaration of what GET /api/decisions' query string contains and the ONE marshaller both composition roots run. DECISION_FILTER_DIMENSIONS is a total Record over keyof DecisionLogFilter so an unregistered dimension is a COMPILE error not a silent gap; parseDecisionLogFilter omits an absent OR empty parameter entirely (a filter can only NARROW - AC-DIM-2); `since` still reaches the ONE domain calendar gate (DEF-ROC-052 unregressed, now one hop along the delegation); and an UNRECOGNISED parameter is DROPPED with the rest of the filter still applied plus a structured caller-data-4xx line naming the parameter and never its value (AC-DIM-6 / delta 021 FAULT-3, the one NEW detector this delta owes). No allow-list of device or status values anywhere - AC-DIM-4"]
    readApiFilter --> decisionFilterQuery
    azureFunctionsHost --> decisionFilterQuery
    decisionFilterQuery --> calendarDate
    decisionFilterQuery --> decisionLogQueryPort

    %% CHANGED BY UC-ROC-113 (server half): decisionFilterQuery (new),
    %% readApiFilter + azureFunctionsHost (both reduced to a delegation — they now
    %% contribute NO dimension name of their own, which is what makes the parity
    %% structural), decisionLogQueryPort (+device on DecisionLogFilter),
    %% tableStoreQuery (+a `device eq` odata clause and +1 predicate in the pure,
    %% authoritative projectDecisionRows).
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: calendarDate (unchanged — it is REACHED one hop
    %% further along, not altered), tableStore/consumer/pipeline (NO write-side
    %% change: `device` was already a required stored column, which is the whole
    %% reason this dimension is the cheap one and UC-114's derived alertStatus is not).
    classDef uc113changed fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px;
    class decisionFilterQuery,readApiFilter,azureFunctionsHost,decisionLogQueryPort,tableStoreQuery uc113changed;

    %% ── UC-ROC-113, browser half — the dimension reaches the SPA end to end ──────
    %% The server half alone is invisible to an operator. What makes `device` a
    %% real dimension is that ONE registry (`decisionView`'s FILTER_DIMENSIONS,
    %% landed by UC-ROC-112) now drives EVERY place a dimension has to appear:
    %% the toolbar control (already registry-driven), `isFilterActive`/Clear
    %% (already), and — added here — the OBSERVED option values, the query string
    %% and the re-query key.
    %%
    %% THE TWO NEWLY REGISTRY-DRIVEN PLACES ARE THE ONES THAT FAIL SILENTLY.
    %% `decisionApi.buildDecisionsUrl` is the SINGLE crossing from filter state to
    %% port call (there is no client-side array filtering anywhere on this
    %% surface), so a dimension shown in the toolbar and missing there moves the
    %% control, announces a new count, and returns the same unnarrowed rows — it
    %% LOOKS like it works and disagrees with the breakdown that sent the operator
    %% there (FAULT-5). `useDecisions.filterKey` is the silent other half: the URL
    %% narrows correctly but the effect does not re-run, leaving the PREVIOUS
    %% dimension's rows on screen. Both now iterate FILTER_DIMENSIONS.
    %%
    %% AND `observedFilterValues` REPLACES `distinctSites`' single-dimension role.
    %% `siteOptions: string[]` became `observedOptions: Partial<Record<dimension,
    %% string[]>>` on decisionToolbar/decisionPage, and decisionContainer
    %% accumulates the union PER DIMENSION. A `deviceOptions` prop beside
    %% `siteOptions` would have been the enumeration defect FILTER_DIMENSIONS
    %% exists to remove, reintroduced one layer down.
    %%
    %% DEPICTED-SOURCE COST, STATED RATHER THAN ASSUMED AWAY: delta 021 §1.5 says
    %% "UC-113/114 then touch NO depicted file". That is FALSE for this UC and the
    %% reason is the generalisation above — decisionContainer, decisionPage and
    %% decisionToolbar are all in captures.json's depicted set (P0.4). The offline
    %% rot arm is unaffected (DEF-ROC-135 made it hash at capturedFromBuildSha, so
    %% it describes the build it names); the LIVE arm reds after the next deploy
    %% and owes ONE re-capture, which costs one real PPSM publish and one real Jira
    %% ticket. One re-capture, not three: 113's whole surface lands together.
    class decisionView,decisionApi,useDecisions,decisionToolbar,decisionPage,decisionContainer uc113changed;

    %% ── UC-ROC-113, the SURFACE — volumes by Device, each row a live route ───────
    %% @alias breakdownTable=dashboard-components-BreakdownTable,breakdownTable
    breakdownTable["dashboard/components/BreakdownTable<br/>UC-ROC-113 NEW: the Device breakdown region on Overview - one row per DISTINCT stored device value in the loaded window with its count, busiest first, each row a live route to the Decision Log pre-filtered to that device. AC-113-5 SETTLES the UC's own open presentation question ('ideally either'): a real 2-D table with thead+tbody is the MINIMUM and a chart is an OPTIONAL addition that may never be a SUBSTITUTE, because a canvas/SVG chart removes the table's testability and its screen-reader semantics. The interaction MIRRORS NeedsAttentionTable attribute for attribute (same house primitives, row-as-activator on click/Enter/Space with Space preventDefault, same focus-visible token) - that treatment was already designed and accepted for this exact surface in UC-ROC-046 and a second idiom on one screen is a new thing to learn for no gain. onNavigate is OPTIONAL: absent, rows are plain trs with no tabindex and no handler, so there is never a focusable control that does nothing. THE EMPTY CASE IS A NAMED STATE INSIDE THE SAME LABELLED REGION (AC-113-3) - never an empty table, never a phantom zero-count row, and the heading does not vanish when the period is quiet. Labelled 'Device' not 'Device Type' per OD-ROC-004 (defaulted, decide-by 2026-09-01): the gate measured 9 raw values with three near-duplicate pairs and PPSM's DeviceDataDto has Device (string) and NO type field, so 'Device Type' would name a taxonomy that does not exist and make nine correct rows look like a broken six. NOT a depicted source"]
    overviewPage --> breakdownTable
    breakdownTable --> overviewStats
    breakdownTable --> decisionView
    breakdownTable -. "UC-113: a row emits a ViewIntent upward" .-> viewIntent

    %% CHANGED BY UC-ROC-113 (the surface): breakdownTable (new), overviewStats
    %% (+breakdownBy/deviceBreakdown — the delta named it "the natural home" and
    %% marked it UNCHANGED by the SEAM, which was true of UC-112 and is no longer
    %% true here), overviewPage (ReadyBody hosts the breakdown between the tiles
    %% and needs-attention).
    %%
    %% THE AGGREGATION IS CLIENT-SIDE AND THE ACCEPTANCE FORCES IT, which is worth
    %% recording because product asked it as an open architecture question and it
    %% is not one: AC-113-4 requires the breakdown's record set to be the SAME set
    %% the tiles are already showing, so a server-side aggregate would be a second
    %% fetch and a SECOND DERIVATION of one fact (EXP-047) — a direct AC-113-4
    %% violation. The FILTER half is the opposite and equally forced: the Decision
    %% Log's "no client-side array filtering" invariant is stated in four places
    %% and the drill-down has to compose with site/since, which are server-side.
    %% So the count folds `state.records` and the drill-down narrows at the port,
    %% and they agree because the breakdown row's RAW value is what becomes
    %% DecisionLogFilter.device — one value, not two derivations (AC-DIM-5).
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: statTiles and needsAttention (untouched — the
    %% breakdown is a sibling region in the same column, folding the same array),
    %% appShell/viewIntent/decisionContainer (UC-112's channel is CONSUMED here,
    %% not changed — a second navigation path would have been the EXP-047
    %% two-writers shape on the app's single view slot, which is exactly why this
    %% UC depends on UC-112 rather than merely sharing files with it).
    class breakdownTable,overviewStats,overviewPage uc113changed;

    %% ── UC-ROC-114, server half — Alert Status is DERIVED at the read boundary ──
    %% @alias derivedAlertStatus=app-src-domain-derivedAlertStatus,derivedAlertStatus
    derivedAlertStatus["app/domain/derivedAlertStatus<br/>UC-ROC-114 NEW (delta 021 RULING 2 section 2.4): the ONE derivation of what Alert Status a decision record's event reports - deriveAlertStatus(event), pure, total, imports nothing. DERIVED AT THE READ BOUNDARY, NEVER A STORED COLUMN: a column can only be written going forward, so the 64 rows already in the deployed log would have none, the breakdown (which counts the blob, all rows) would permanently disagree with the drill-down (which would filter the column), and the only remedy would be a prod-DATA backfill - a guaranteed AC-114-2 violation, refused. IT BRANCHES ON NO STATUS STRING (AC-DIM-4, the gate's explicit BUILD GATE): no allow-list of the six values delta 021 measured - the live log now carries a SEVENTH, CLOSE - no case folding (Offline vs ONLINE are both real upstream facts) and no Unknown bucket. ABSENT MEANS ABSENT: a record whose event yields no status gets no key, no row and no bucket, and that exclusion is NEVER keyed on outcome - the live log's own outcome not-handled record REPROB2608201034/BTP1 is classification recognised with status Paper Out and IS included (AC-114-3, amended). MIRRORS dashboard classifyEventForDisplay's recognised branch condition for condition; the two units cannot import each other, so the agreement is pinned in BOTH tiers against ONE committed real capture (the statusVocabularyMirror precedent). NOT a depicted source"]
    tableStoreQuery --> derivedAlertStatus

    %% CHANGED BY UC-ROC-114 (server half): derivedAlertStatus (new),
    %% tableStoreQuery (toRecord parses the event ONCE and derives alertStatus
    %% from that same object, so the field and the blob cannot disagree),
    %% decisionRecord (+the derived optional alertStatus field, with no writer).
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: tableStore/consumer/pipeline — there is NO
    %% write-side change at all, which is the whole content of the §2.4 ruling.
    %% ── UC-ROC-114, the `status` FILTER DIMENSION — derived, so no odata clause ──
    %% decisionFilterQuery gains `status` in the one REGISTERED record (typed
    %% Record<keyof DecisionLogFilter, ...>, so the port key and the parser cannot
    %% drift), decisionLogQueryPort gains DecisionLogFilter.status, and
    %% tableStoreQuery applies it AFTER the mapping because there is no column to
    %% test on the row. BOTH composition roots (readApiFilter, azureFunctionsHost)
    %% pick the dimension up with NO edit at all — that is UC-113's registry
    %% paying for itself, and it is why AC-DIM-1's parity here is by construction.
    %%
    %% THE ONE THING THAT COULD BREAK ON THE DEPLOYED HOST ONLY: an odata clause
    %% naming `alertStatus`/`status` would narrow the FETCH to a column that does
    %% not exist, emptying every drill-down while the pure core (which re-applies
    %% every predicate itself) stayed green. Pinned at the source offline AND
    %% round-tripped through real Azurite in tests/acceptance/uc114-status-filter-azurite.
    %% ── UC-ROC-114, browser half — the dimension reaches the SPA end to end ─────
    %% decisionView gains the DERIVED alertStatus on DecisionRecordDTO, the
    %% `status` key on DecisionFilter, and — the load-bearing bit — a `recordField`
    %% on FilterDimensionSpec. `status` is the FIRST dimension whose wire parameter
    %% and record FIELD have different names (the port's key is `status`; the
    %% record's derived field is `alertStatus`), and an observed-values helper
    %% keyed blindly on dim.key would have read a `record.status` that does not
    %% exist and rendered a SILENTLY EMPTY dropdown beside a breakdown showing
    %% seven rows. Everything else — the toolbar control, Clear, isFilterActive,
    %% the query string, the re-query key — needed NO edit at all, which is
    %% UC-ROC-112/113's registry paying for itself a second time.
    %% ── UC-ROC-114, the SURFACE — volumes by Alert Status, each row a live route ─
    %% @alias breakdownDimensions=dashboard-components-breakdownDimensions,breakdownDimensions
    breakdownDimensions["dashboard/components/breakdownDimensions<br/>UC-ROC-114 NEW: WHAT A BREAKDOWN DIMENSION IS, as data - id (test-hook prefix), label (heading AND value-column header AND accessible-name lead, so the three cannot disagree), unit noun, the FOLD, the DecisionFilter key a row's value becomes, and the NAMED EMPTY STATE as a function of the loaded records. BreakdownTable was Device-specific; a second near-identical component would have been the enumeration defect FILTER_DIMENSIONS exists to remove, reintroduced one layer up - two places that must agree about how a breakdown row behaves with nothing red if only one changes. THE DIMENSION PROP IS REQUIRED, NOT DEFAULTED (EXP-121 required-not-optional applied to a presentation seam): a default meaning Device is exactly how a third breakdown gets added later and silently renders the wrong fold under the right heading. THE EMPTY STATE IS A FUNCTION BECAUSE THE TWO DIMENSIONS GENUINELY DIFFER: device is a required stored column so its breakdown is empty only when the period is; alertStatus is DERIVED and really is absent on real records (14 of the deployed log's 64), so a period can hold events and still have nothing to break down - saying 'no events in this period' would then be a LIE, which is AC-114-4. The filterKey is the PORT's key (status), never the record's field name (alertStatus): sending the field name would be dropped by the read boundary as an unrecognised parameter and the drill-down would show everything. NOT a depicted source"]
    breakdownTable --> breakdownDimensions
    breakdownDimensions --> overviewStats
    breakdownDimensions --> decisionView
    overviewPage --> breakdownDimensions

    %% CHANGED BY UC-ROC-114 (the surface): breakdownDimensions (new),
    %% breakdownTable (parameterised by its dimension; every testid, heading,
    %% unit noun and empty state now comes from the spec), overviewStats
    %% (+alertStatusBreakdown - ONE SELECTOR over UC-113's generic breakdownBy,
    %% whose absent-value rule was written for a dimension that could never
    %% exercise it precisely because this one would), overviewPage (ReadyBody
    %% hosts BOTH breakdown regions, Device then Alert Status, in the same
    %% in-flow column).
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: statTiles, needsAttention, appShell, viewIntent,
    %% decisionContainer, decisionToolbar, decisionApi, useDecisions — every one
    %% of them picks this dimension up with NO edit, off the registry UC-112/113
    %% landed. That is the point of the two predecessors and it is why this UC,
    %% costed at 1.2 for nested-blob work, reduced to one derivation, one
    %% registry entry, one selector and one spec.
    classDef uc114changed fill:#ede7f6,stroke:#5e35b1,stroke-width:2px;
    class derivedAlertStatus,tableStoreQuery,decisionRecord,decisionFilterQuery,decisionLogQueryPort,decisionView,breakdownDimensions,breakdownTable,overviewStats,overviewPage uc114changed;

    %% ── DEF-ROC-149, the ENGINEERING EXIT GATE (process §F11) ────────────────
    %% @alias designQualityGate=scripts-design-quality-gate,designQualityGate
    designQualityGate["scripts/design-quality-gate.mjs DEF-ROC-149 NEW<br/>make exit-gate - THE THREE-LIMB EXIT CONDITION ON THE ENGINEERING STEP, before the tester takes over. It is an ACCOUNTABILITY change, not an integration one: AeroCloudSystems/CodeAnalysisTools was ALREADY WIRED here (code-analysis.yml, every push to main and weekly, already excluding items/*, already detecting generated files) and it UPLOADED AN ARTIFACT AND GATED NOTHING, so nobody ever read it - OI-ROC-014/IMP-021/DEF-ROC-140/DEF-ROC-146, a control that exists and is never consulted, arriving a fifth time. LIMB 1 change-coupling between SOURCE files ratcheted DOWN; the 12 of 15 reported pairs that couple code to a DOC or to the change-impact model are printed but NOT ratcheted, because this process REQUIRES that co-change and a gate that reds on compliance is one everybody learns to ignore. LIMB 2 coverage as a REGRESSION DETECTOR - did it get worse, never is it high enough; assertNoTargetFigures REFUSES to run against a baseline that grows a target/minimum/threshold key, which mechanises v127's ruling instead of writing it down. LIMB 3 every test attaches to a node of the AUTHORED variation graph (product/variations/), rooted persona-job-use-case-variation-test; a test on no node is inside-out debt, two tests on one node is a duplicate, a node with no test is a gap. THREE OUTCOMES not two: PASS / REGRESSION / a hard throw when a tier produced NO summary at all, because an unrun tier is not a clean one. NOT in deploy-test's needs: limb 1 reads FULL GIT HISTORY, which no paths: filter can watch, so gating the deploy on it would be the 25th DEF-ROC-145 instance"]
    %% @alias analysisConfig=quality-analysis-config,analysisConfig
    analysisConfig["quality/analysis-config.json DEF-ROC-149 NEW<br/>THE ONE PLACE the CodeAnalysisTools flags live, and a REQUIRED dependency of both lanes rather than a convenience. code-analysis.yml reads it with jq into the action's with: inputs; make exit-gate reads it into the same tool's docker image (the action ships Linux binaries only, so macOS runs the published image - same binary, same tag, same flags). The gate's own suite PINS that the workflow does not inline the values. It also carries trunk: main, because the tool reads git log --all and --all is not the same ref set in the two lanes (measured: 1040 commits / 3 authors in a developer checkout carrying 22 refs/remotes/pr/*, 1021 / 2 on trunk alone) - so both lanes clone a single-branch mirror first. Widening its ignore list is the OI-ROC-006 anti-pattern and an automatic kill on EXP-ROC-014"]
    %% @alias qualityBaseline=quality-baseline,qualityBaseline
    qualityBaseline["quality/baseline.json DEF-ROC-149 NEW<br/>THE RATCHET FLOORS. Every number is a MEASUREMENT, never a target. Written only by the gate; a passing run whose measurement is better LOWERS a floor, and --write-baseline REFUSES to raise one without both an explicit flag and a stated reason. First measured 2026-08-29: codeCouplings 3, crossModuleCodeCouplings 0, coverage 89.0/82.8 app - 90.7/90.8 dashboard - 58.0/63.8 injector (the FIRST coverage numbers this project has ever had; no package carried a provider before), casesWithNoVariation 4023 of 4027"]
    %% @alias variationGraph=product-variations,variationGraph
    variationGraph["product/variations/ DEF-ROC-149 NEW<br/>THE AUTHORED VARIATION GRAPH, one file per use-case (disjoint files never merge-conflict; one big graph file would be a co-owned append target, the class that has silently lost and silently duplicated committed work in this tree). AUTHORED FROM THE ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA, NEVER DERIVED FROM THE TESTS - a graph derived from what the tests happen to do agrees with itself by construction, which is §17i and this project's dominant failure family. A test declares its node IN ITS TITLE (@UC-ROC-nnn/...) and the inventory is built from THE RUNNER'S OWN REPORT of what it ran, never from parsing spec sources, because IMP-021 and DEF-ROC-140 were both gates blind to a construct their regex never looked at. SEEDED, NOT MIGRATED: UC-ROC-093 is the worked example (6 nodes, 4 certified offline, 2 declared in tiers this inventory does not cover); the other 115 use-cases are the ratchet's work"]
    designQualityGate --> analysisConfig
    designQualityGate --> qualityBaseline
    designQualityGate --> variationGraph

    %% CHANGED BY DEF-ROC-149: the four nodes above are new. Behaviour-changed and
    %% marked with them: nothing in the RUNTIME graph — this item adds no runtime
    %% edge and touches no deployed code path. What it does change is the
    %% engineering step's exit condition, which is why it is modelled here beside
    %% the other executable gates (notHandledProbe, joinQuery, sinkRenderer)
    %% rather than left as an unmodelled script.
    classDef def149changed fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#e65100,stroke-width:2px;
    class designQualityGate,analysisConfig,qualityBaseline,variationGraph def149changed;

    %% ── DEF-ROC-148 — a REQUIRED configuration value with NO DECLARATION AT ALL ──
    %% @alias newTypeIssueType=config-newTypeIssueType
    newTypeIssueType["config/newTypeIssueType DEF-ROC-148 NEW<br/>THE ONE DERIVATION OF 'can UC-ROC-007's new-message-type ticket be raised at all'. The ticket's Jira ISSUE-TYPE ID shipped as a SOURCE LITERAL '10001' in JiraApiAdapter - the id Jira hands 'Task' in a default company-managed scheme. ASKED AT THE SOURCE 2026-08-29 (new read-only local/jira-issuetypes-check -> GET createmeta/ROC/issuetypes): project ROC's creatable types are 10375 Support Incident, 11829 PPSM Alert and three sub-tasks. 10001 IS NOT AMONG THEM, so every create the deployed host ever attempted was a GUARANTEED HTTP 400 and a delivered use-case had NEVER ONCE WORKED in the only environment ROC has. An issue-type id is an EXTERNAL fact about a system we do not own, so it is CONFIGURATION obtained by asking, never a plausible literal. THREE ORDINARY PROPERTIES HID IT and each is answered here. (1) SYNTACTICALLY VALID so nothing local rejected it -> the placeholder is refused BY NAME, not merely absent-checked, so re-introducing the guess can never silently ship. (2) The only override was a CODE EDIT so no deployment step, app setting or drift check could ask whether it was set - expected-app-settings.json cannot flag a setting never declared to exist -> it is now the app setting ROC_JIRA_NEW_TYPE_ISSUE_TYPE_ID, stamped by deploy-ROC.yml, declared in the SSOT, carried by devProfile at the SAME value. (3) The failure surfaced as a RUNTIME 400 which until DEF-ROC-144 was swallowed by the very throw that lost the event - THE DEFECT CONCEALED ITS OWN TRIGGER -> an absent/placeholder/malformed value is a DECLARED not-configured state: newTypeUnconfiguredLine is logged LOUDLY once at composition (the telemetry.dash0.disabled shape), jiraEgressStatus reports it on /api/health, and the adapter refuses PRE-FLIGHT. NO DEFAULT, fail-safe CLOSED (v124): undefined MEANS not configured, never 'send it and see'. THREE READERS ONE DERIVATION (EXP-047) - the startup declaration, the health posture and the pre-flight refusal cannot disagree about whether the capability works or why it does not. OI-ROC-014 INVERTED: there a declared control with no reader, here a required value with no declaration."]:::def148changed
    hostJira --> newTypeIssueType
    selectJira --> newTypeIssueType
    jiraEgressStatus --> newTypeIssueType
    jiraApi --> newTypeIssueType

    %% classDef def148changed marks what DEF-ROC-148 changes, and the marks are the
    %% tester's test-plan input. jiraApi: the '10001' default is GONE and
    %% createNewTypeTicket gains a PRE-FLIGHT guard (the assertDropdown shape) plus the
    %% NOT_CONFIGURED_CATEGORY it throws. hostJira / selectJira: both real composition
    %% roots now RESOLVE the setting and DECLARE an unusable one; selectHostJira also
    %% gains fetchImpl/tokenUrl passthrough so the DEPLOYED branch can be driven
    %% end-to-end with no live socket. jiraEgressStatus + healthHttp: the posture gains
    %% newTypeTicket/newTypeTicketReason, ALWAYS PRESENT unlike degraded - absence-as-
    %% reassurance is exactly what the last months looked like. raiseFailure: the
    %% refused-category ENUMERATION is widened by internal-not-configured, deliberately -
    %% nothing is sent, so it is the most certain member of that set, and leaving it out
    %% would make the consumer KEEP the first-sighting marker and render UC-ROC-007's
    %% ticket unraisable for that type FOR EVER even after the setting was corrected
    %% (DEF-ROC-049's burnt claim, re-created by omission). devProfile: carries the same
    %% value as the deploy stamp so a local run and the deployed host cannot diverge.
    %% selectDemoJira is marked because its OMISSION is now a DECLARED lane decision
    %% (v124): the demo targets a different project where ROC's id means nothing, so its
    %% new-type create refuses pre-flight, loudly, by design rather than by accident.
    classDef def148changed fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#0d47a1,stroke-width:2px;
    class newTypeIssueType,jiraApi,hostJira,selectJira,jiraEgressStatus,healthHttp,raiseFailure,devProfile,selectDemoJira def148changed;


    %% ── DEF-ROC-109 — ONE union, TWO hand-kept derivations, and the second was forgotten twice ──
    %% @alias appOutcomeUnionReader=dashboard-fixtures-appDecisionOutcomes,appOutcomeUnionReader
    appOutcomeUnionReader["dashboard/fixtures/appDecisionOutcomes DEF-ROC-109 NEW<br/>THE BROWSER'S ONLY HONEST READING OF THE OUTCOME UNION. TEST-ONLY (reads a source file off disk; never imported by anything that ships, and the coverage config excludes the directory). It reads OUTCOME_CLASSIFICATION out of app/domain/decisionRecord's OWN SOURCE and returns its keys - that map and not the `type` declaration, because it is typed Record&lt;DecisionOutcome,...&gt; so the compiler already refuses both a missing member and a non-member, which makes its keys the union EXACTLY. WHY A SOURCE READ AND NOT AN IMPORT: the dashboard build is deliberately free of the app's Node package (delta 003 decision 2), which is why DecisionRecordDTO MIRRORS DecisionRecord rather than importing it - so this is the established cross-compilation-unit mirror idiom already used by AC-DIM-1 (decision.uc113.test.ts) and def075ReadBoundaryColumnParity. WHAT HAND-COPYING COST, MEASURED: decision.def088.test.ts hand-copied the union as a NINE-member literal and pinned its own length at nine, while the union had held TEN since 2026-08-14. So the guard whose stated purpose was `the gap cannot silently reopen` certified totality over a list already short a member, and read green while four malformed-identity records rendered through the unknown-outcome fallback on the deployed screen. It THROWS rather than returning empty if the block or the entries are not findable, because a reader that silently finds nothing makes every totality assertion vacuous - the IMP-021/DEF-ROC-140 class, which this project has now registered eight times"]:::def109changed
    appOutcomeUnionReader --> decisionRecord

    %% classDef def109changed marks what DEF-ROC-109 changes, and the marks are the
    %% tester's test-plan input.
    %%   decisionView: CODE-CHANGED. OUTCOME_CATALOGUE is the single declaration;
    %%     OUTCOME_BADGE and OUTCOME_OPTIONS are both derived from it. Three outcomes
    %%     become filterable for the first time (cleared, resolved, malformed-identity)
    %%     and malformed-identity gains a designed badge (pink / "Rejected" - the one
    %%     house Badge colour no other outcome uses, same <hue>-100 fill / <hue>-800 text
    %%     pairing as every other entry). Fold-tolerance is UNCHANGED: an outcome that is
    %%     genuinely unknown still falls back to the grey raw word.
    %%   decisionToolbar, decisionPage: BEHAVIOUR-CHANGED WITHOUT A CODE CHANGE - the
    %%     Outcome dropdown renders three more options and the table paints one more
    %%     designed badge, both purely because their data source grew. Marked so
    %%     `make impacted-tests` reports them, since a change that alters what an
    %%     operator SEES while leaving the component source byte-identical is exactly
    %%     the kind the model exists to expose (the DEF-ROC-076 shape).
    %%   appOutcomeUnionReader: NEW, above.
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: nothing on the SERVER. The read boundary always
    %% accepted any outcome token and was verified live on 2026-08-29 answering
    %% ?outcome=cleared / resolved / malformed-identity with exactly 8 / 6 / 4 records.
    %% The defect was entirely in what the browser was willing to ask for.
    classDef def109changed fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#4a148c,stroke-width:2px;
    class appOutcomeUnionReader,decisionView,decisionToolbar,decisionPage def109changed;

    %% ---------------------------------------------------------------- OI-ROC-010
    %% THE CORPUS DIFFERENTIAL — a fixture is never TIGHTER than the capture beside it.
    %% @alias fixtureCorporaContract=src-contracts-fixture-corpora,fixtureCorporaContract
    fixtureCorporaContract["src/contracts/fixture-corpora.json OI-ROC-010 NEW<br/>THE REGISTRY a fixture's claim is COMPUTED against. Per boundary: the AUTHORED corpora (each with the CLAIM it is held to), the real CAPTURES, and the two DECLARED field lists that are design acts rather than heuristics - keyFields (D3 runs on these only; messageId is half the decision RowKey ticks|messageId, the append idempotency key AND the React row key, so a repeat is a collision three ways over) and enumFields (D4). NOTHING HERE IS A LABEL AN AUTHOR WRITES ABOUT THEIR OWN FIXTURE: sampleDecisions.ts ALREADY carried that label - reconciled against a REAL /api/decisions capture - and it was wrong beneath 755 green tests while the deployed screen was broken. A declaration by the same author in the same sitting cannot come back negative because nothing computes it, so the registry records only POINTERS a machine dereferences. THE #POINTER SUFFIX IS LOAD-BEARING: the three captures do NOT share a top-level key (response, response, records), so a resolver assuming one shape reads ZERO records from def093 and the gate passes vacuously. DATA, never imported by any runtime, never packaged - same posture as roc-test-marker.json, simulator-publish-body.json and quarantined-paths.json"]:::oi010changed
    %% @alias corpusDifferential=dashboard-fixtures-corpusDifferential,corpusDifferential
    corpusDifferential["dashboard/fixtures/corpusDifferential OI-ROC-010 NEW<br/>THE ENGINE, pure and dependency-free so its own tests can drive it with synthetic corpora. Five dimensions over two independently-authored corpora: D1 shape (types_R subset of types_A), D2 absence (reality sometimes OMITS it, so the fixture must too), D3 key multiplicity on DECLARED keyFields only, D4 vocabulary and D5 path coverage as down-only ratchets. null and array are their OWN type tags, never folded into object, because String(null)/String([]) are the same family of bug as String({}) - literally DEF-ROC-094 on 100% of deployed records. A path under an ABSENT PARENT is UNDETERMINED rather than absent, so D2 does not cascade through every optional sub-tree and cry wolf. Arrays are LEAVES; element shapes are out of scope and named as such. Also owns the registry's PURE claims: registryViolations (delta 022 section 2 - a boundary may be declared uncapturable ONLY if it has NO capturable downstream, which is the rule that would have refused invocation.ts's original fixtures) and harvestedSubsetViolations (a corpus that narrows BY DESIGN is held to harvestedness instead, checked BOTH ways so a synthetic mark cannot become an escape hatch)"]:::oi010changed
    %% @alias oi010CorpusGate=dashboard-fixtures-oi010CorpusDifferential,oi010CorpusGate
    oi010CorpusGate["dashboard/fixtures/oi010CorpusDifferential + corpusDifferential.test OI-ROC-010 NEW<br/>THE GATE plus its NON-VACUITY SUITE, and the second half is what stops the fix being the defect. D1 is GREEN on today's real corpora (the live [object Object] rows arrive already flattened to a string), so without five synthetic pairs proving each dimension CAN fire plus a clean pair proving the engine cannot pass by always failing, D1 would be the read-healthy-does-nothing control INSIDE the fix for read-healthy-does-nothing controls. IT CAME BACK NEGATIVE UNSEEDED ON ITS FIRST RUN: D3 messageId (the capture repeats a value 22x; every authored value UNIQUE) and five D2 absences (four live records carry an event blob with no classification/node/device/raw/timestamps key at all). Captures are READ FROM DISK, never imported, keeping the cross-package rule (a cross-root import shifts tsc's computed common root and dark-deploys - DEF-ROC-086). Prints every capture's capturedTs, age, record count and refusal-lane observation count on every run: zero refusals is the HEALTHY case so it can never be an alarm, which is the only way TriggerMessageIdUnreadable's being unobserved since 2026-08-26 becomes a reading rather than a belief"]:::oi010changed
    %% @alias fixtureCorpusBaseline=quality-fixture-corpus-baseline,fixtureCorpusBaseline
    fixtureCorpusBaseline["quality/fixture-corpus-baseline.json OI-ROC-010 NEW<br/>THE DOWN-ONLY FLOORS for D4/D5 and for unregisteredFixtureFiles (16 today, across two of ROC's five fixture directories). ITS OWN FILE, not quality/baseline.json, deliberately: that file says in its own header it is written and tightened ONLY by design-quality-gate.mjs and is rewritten wholesale, and two writers on one ratchet store is the disagreement-by-construction shape EXP-047 retires. The gate TIGHTENS these automatically when it measures better and has no operation that raises one. delta 022 section 12 names the STALL of unregisteredFixtureFiles as what would falsify the whole direction: if it does not fall, the gate has certified one boundary and become a decoration"]:::oi010changed
    oi010CorpusGate --> corpusDifferential
    oi010CorpusGate --> fixtureCorporaContract
    oi010CorpusGate --> fixtureCorpusBaseline
    oi010CorpusGate --> decisionView

    %% classDef oi010changed marks what OI-ROC-010 ADDS or CHANGES, and the marks are
    %% the tester's test-plan input.
    %%   fixtureCorporaContract, corpusDifferential, oi010CorpusGate,
    %%     fixtureCorpusBaseline: NEW, above.
    %%   designQualityGate: CODE-CHANGED. A variation root may now be ANY tracked work
    %%     item, not only a UC- one, in knownUseCaseIds AND in NODE_REF. It accepted
    %%     UC- only, so a defect's or an open-item's tests could attach to nothing BY
    %%     CONSTRUCTION and then counted for ever as inside-out debt nobody could pay
    %%     off. Measured before widening: of 4,042 inventory cases, ZERO gain a node
    %%     ref under the wider pattern, so it admits new roots without reinterpreting
    %%     one existing title. The reality check is unchanged - a root nobody wrote is
    %%     still refused.
    %%   variationGraph: BEHAVIOUR-CHANGED WITHOUT A CODE CHANGE - it now holds its
    %%     first non-use-case root (OI-ROC-010, 24 nodes, 24 tests, no gap and no
    %%     duplicate). Marked so `make impacted-tests` reports it.
    %%   decisionView: NOT code-changed, but it is the DTO the differential profiles,
    %%     so the edge is drawn to it rather than left implicit.
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: nothing on the SERVER and nothing in any deployed
    %% artefact. This is an offline computation over two committed corpora; it needs no
    %% emulator, no credential and no network (delta 022 section 10).
    classDef oi010changed fill:#e0f2f1,stroke:#00695c,stroke-width:2px;
    class fixtureCorporaContract,corpusDifferential,oi010CorpusGate,fixtureCorpusBaseline,designQualityGate,variationGraph oi010changed;

    %% ---------------------------------------------------------------- UC-ROC-115
    %% THE INFO DESTINATION — a fifth top-level view, and the browser's SECOND
    %% mirror of the pipeline's own Alert-Status vocabulary.
    %% @alias infoPage=dashboard-components-InfoPage,infoPage
    infoPage["dashboard/components/InfoPage UC-ROC-115 NEW<br/>The Info destination: a meaning-only explainer for the six in-scope PPSM Alert Statuses. PRESENTATIONAL BY DESIGN - no port, no fetch, no state, so there is no loading/empty/error state to render and no derived fact it could fail to establish (its screen-gate entry says exactly that as its noClaims reason). It ITERATES the browser mirror ALERT_STATUS_TOKENS, so the order on screen IS the constant's order and there is no second list; its content map is Record&lt;AlertStatusToken,string&gt;, so a SEVENTH token is a COMPILE error until someone writes what it means and a stale extra key is a compile error too - AC-115-5's anti-drift claim is certified by the type system, not by a runtime assertion. THREE THINGS THE BUILD FOUND. (1) The status name is a th scope=row inside an INLINE span: the th stretches to the row and the Unknown row is three sentences tall, so measuring the CELL calls a one-word label two lines and makes the DEF-ROC-057 no-wrap acceptance unmeasurable. (2) The house table root's muted gray-500 is BARRED from the meaning column - it passes every AA text check and reads washed-out, and the meaning text is the whole point of the page. (3) main carries tabIndex=0 because OI-ROC-009's assembled-screen axe CAUGHT scrollable-region-focusable here, serious, WCAG 2.1.1, at three of four viewports: this is the FIRST scroll region in the app with no focusable content inside it, every other view holding filters or buttons, so without it the content below the fold was POINTER-ONLY. NOT a depicted source"]:::uc115changed
    appShell --> infoPage
    infoPage --> simulatorViewModel

    %% classDef uc115changed marks what UC-ROC-115 ADDS or CHANGES, and the marks
    %% are the tester's test-plan input.
    %%   infoPage: NEW, above.
    %%   appNav: CODE-CHANGED, and it is the one edit that needed a DECISION rather
    %%     than a diff. It APPENDS a fifth item (Info) LAST, pushed to the
    %%     right-hand gutter by `ml-auto` on that item only; the first four keep
    %%     their order, labels and testids byte-unchanged. UC-ROC-112's AC-SEAM-4
    %%     had pinned this file's sha256 BYTE-IDENTICAL, and its own pin says
    %%     changing it "must be a decision somebody makes, with a re-capture, not a
    %%     drive-by edit" - so the pin now carries the decision record and the old
    %%     hash beside the new one. THE SEAM ITSELF IS UNTOUCHED: onSelect still
    %%     emits a bare AppView and App still adapts it into a filterless intent,
    %%     which is what AC-SEAM-4 is actually about. RE-CAPTURE OWED at the next
    %%     deploy (captures.json depicts a four-item nav; the OFFLINE rot arm reads
    %%     the capture build out of git and is unaffected, the LIVE arm is already
    %%     deferred under DEF-ROC-141).
    %%   appShell: CODE-CHANGED. AppView widens by one member and renderView gains
    %%     one case. NO new state slot: an Info arrival is filterless like every
    %%     other nav arrival, so UC-ROC-112's one-slot AC-SEAM-1 is untouched.
    %%   simulatorViewModel: CODE-CHANGED. It gains ALERT_STATUS_TOKENS, a SECOND
    %%     mirror surface beside STATUS_VALUES, bound to the app's own constant
    %%     from BOTH sides by the existing pins so editing one side alone reds the
    %%     suite. It is a SEPARATE plain literal rather than a spread inside
    %%     STATUS_VALUES, deliberately: both pins parse STATUS_VALUES as SOURCE
    %%     TEXT and a spread would break the parser. And it is NOT named
    %%     ALERT_STATUS_VALUES - that name is the Jira customfield_12074 dropdown
    %%     set in JiraApiAdapter, a different list on a channel ROC does not
    %%     consume.
    %% THE COST, NAMED RATHER THAN DISCOVERED LATER: a nav round trip DISCARDS the
    %% origin view's state. The shell mounts exactly one view and AC-SEAM-1 makes
    %% every nav arrival structurally unseeded, so a responder who filtered the
    %% Decision Log and stepped out to read a status returns UNFILTERED, mid-triage,
    %% with no signal. Accepted for this UC and pinned as a variation node so it is
    %% measured rather than a surprise; handed to UC-ROC-116 as a BINDING design
    %% input - a contextual "what does this mean?" link that is a plain nav-switch
    %% throws the filter away at the worst possible moment, so 116 must overlay or
    %% carry a return intent.
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: nothing on the SERVER, no read boundary, no port,
    %% no new house component and no new colour token. `normalise` is the SOURCE of
    %% the vocabulary but is unchanged by this UC - the edge that matters is the
    %% pin, which already exists in both tiers.
    classDef uc115changed fill:#ede7f6,stroke:#4527a0,stroke-width:2px;
    class infoPage,appNav,appShell,simulatorViewModel uc115changed;

    %% ---------------------------------------------------------------- DEF-ROC-167
    %% THE UNPARSEABLE MESSAGE HAD NOWHERE TO BE LOOKED FOR (DEF-ROC-073's FOURTH gate,
    %% wrongly ruled out). Step 1 of the change is the SHARED SEAMS it needs, extracted
    %% before any new behaviour exists so two lanes cannot end up with two answers.
    %% @alias valueShape=domain-valueShape,valueShape
    valueShape["domain/valueShape DEF-ROC-167 NEW (extracted, behaviour-preserving)<br/>THE SHAPE OF A VALUE AND NEVER ITS CONTENT - keys and TYPES only, never a VALUE, because a value on a diagnostic line is uncontrolled cardinality on the log sink and can carry payload text (the rule dash0Metrics states for its labels, applied to lines). It was a PRIVATE helper inside host/invocation (DEF-ROC-112, so the trigger-metadata object nobody could capture would be captured on the next real event); DEF-ROC-167 needs the identical description one layer down for an UNPARSEABLE telemetry body, and a second copy of this reasoning is how two lanes disagree about what may be logged. MOVED, not duplicated: pure, import-free, and the dependency direction is unchanged (host -> domain)"]:::def167changed
    %% @alias reservedIdentity=domain-reservedIdentity,reservedIdentity
    reservedIdentity["domain/reservedIdentity DEF-ROC-167 NEW<br/>IS THIS A NODE? asked as a DOMAIN question instead of asserted as a constant at a read boundary. A quarantined event is a full decision record under a reserved token no real PPSM node can occupy, which is deliberate VISIBILITY (runbook E-CT-04) - but a reserved token is not a NODE, so it must never be offered as a site-pattern draft-test sample, which would be DEF-ROC-030's mangling arriving by the back door. That exclusion was a bare r.node === MALFORMED_IDENTITY_NODE inside TableStorageDecisionLogQuery, one compilation unit from the declaration, with nothing to notice a SECOND reserved identity appearing. DEF-ROC-098 is the measured cost of that exact shape at that exact boundary. Still an enumeration - reserved is a decision somebody makes - but it now sits NEXT TO what it enumerates, so declaring one and forgetting the boundary is one edit, not two files apart"]:::def167changed
    hostInvocation --> valueShape
    reservedIdentity --> identityKey
    tableStoreQuery --> reservedIdentity

    %% @alias unparseableBody=domain-unparseableBody,unparseableBody
    unparseableBody["domain/unparseableBody DEF-ROC-167 NEW<br/>THE MESSAGE WE CANNOT READ NOW HAS SOMEWHERE TO BE LOOKED FOR. The owner asked where to go and look when ROC cannot parse a message off the bus and the honest answer was NOWHERE: consumer/index.ts did `if (!decision) return` with the comment #quot;Malformed envelope: not a telemetry event - nothing to record#quot; and emitted no log line, no record, no counter and no metric. THAT COMMENT'S ASSUMPTION WAS FALSE, which is what makes it a defect rather than a gap - asEnvelope refuses THREE things: a body that is not an object (which on this transport includes a VALID envelope delivered as JSON TEXT, since host/invocation passes the body through), a body matching neither the MassTransit nor the legacy shape, and a body ALMOST the shape with device/data/computer/created missing, non-string or blank-typed = a TRUNCATED REAL PPSM MESSAGE. One if(!decision) folded #quot;we could not read this#quot; together with #quot;this was not for us#quot;, which is DEF-ROC-091's shape named in prose in that very file. Owns the RESERVED __unparseable_body__|rejected identity (constants, so recording can never hit the failure it records), the sha256 row id (deterministic -> a redelivery at the same recording instant is an insert-only no-op), the VERBATIM body bounded at 30,000 chars with rejectedBodyTruncated/rejectedBodyChars DECLARED on the row (Table Storage bounds one String property at 64 KiB, so an unbounded copy would 400 the very append that records the failure), and the log fields, which carry the SHAPE ONLY - keys and types, one nested level, never a value. Deliberately NOT reusing malformed-identity: there the body PARSED and its identity could not be a key (a character-set/mandatory-field contract), here the body could not be read at all (a message-contract or transport-encoding matter) - different remedies, so a distinct outcome, the DEF-ROC-039 rule. NEVER THROWS (Event Hubs redelivery = a poison loop on a message that will never parse, and on this transport the throw also abandons the rest of the batch - DEF-ROC-144, measured live) and NEVER MANGLES (defaulting a field to make it parse would invent a device). node:crypto only, cloud-agnostic"]:::def167changed
    unparseableBody --> decisionRecord
    unparseableBody --> valueShape
    unparseableBody --> identityKey
    pipeline --> unparseableBody
    consumer --> unparseableBody
    reservedIdentity --> unparseableBody

    %% classDef def167changed marks what DEF-ROC-167 changes, and the marks are the
    %% tester's test-plan input.
    %%   valueShape, reservedIdentity: NEW (the entry-gate refactor - shaped to receive
    %%     the change, committed before a line of the new behaviour existed). valueShape
    %%     then gained fieldTypes/fieldShapes/keysTruncated, because KEYS ALONE CANNOT
    %%     DIAGNOSE THIS FAULT: a truncated real message has exactly the keys of a valid
    %%     one and differs only in a TYPE. The DEF-ROC-112 line it already fed gains
    %%     those fields too - additive, and strictly better for the uncaptured
    %%     trigger-metadata shape that line exists to capture.
    %%   unparseableBody: NEW, above.
    %%   pipeline: CODE-CHANGED and its CONTRACT WIDENED. makeDecide no longer returns
    %%     null: `DecideEvent` is now NON-NULLABLE, so the decision is TOTAL over every
    %%     message that arrives and the silent branch is not expressible in the type. It
    %%     MINTS the quarantine record (pure, from the composition-point clock and build
    %%     sha it already holds) and carries it on the new typed EventDecision
    %%     .unparseableBody, the same way unrecognisedType/deviceCodeUnmapped ride.
    %%   consumer: CODE-CHANGED. `if (!decision) return` is GONE, replaced by the
    %%     unparseable-body lane as the FIRST thing decided - an error-level
    %%     structuredLine (shape only) BEFORE the append, then the append, then return
    %%     and checkpoint. Same order and same reasoning as the malformed-IDENTITY gate
    %%     eight lines below it, which had all of this right already.
    %%   decisionRecord: CODE-CHANGED, ADDITIVE. One new DecisionOutcome member
    %%     (`unparseable-body`, non-lifecycle) - schemaVersion stays 0, the fold is
    %%     untouched and still tolerates every stored outcome.
    %%   decisionView: CODE-CHANGED. One OUTCOME_CATALOGUE entry, from which the badge
    %%     map AND the filter dropdown are both derived (DEF-ROC-109), so the new
    %%     outcome is filterable and labelled in the same edit. It SHARES `pink` with
    %%     malformed-identity on purpose: the catalogue has exhausted the house Badge
    %%     variants proven to paint, and reaching for an unproven one to win a distinct
    %%     hue is the ROC C4 class this project has taken three live a11y rejects on.
    %%     Colour is redundant; the LABEL ("Unparseable" vs "Rejected") carries it.
    %%   tableStoreQuery: BEHAVIOUR-PRESERVING REDIRECT of the recent-nodes exclusion
    %%     from the constant to the domain predicate - and then the second reserved node
    %%     joins the registry, which is the whole reason the redirect came first.
    %%   hostInvocation: CODE-CHANGED, behaviour-preserving - shapeOf is now imported.
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: no port changed (the record goes through the existing
    %% AlertStatePort.append), the READ boundary needed no change at all (isDecisionRow
    %% is a POSITIVE shape predicate since DEF-ROC-098, so a decision row in a reserved
    %% partition nobody had written yet is projectable BY CONSTRUCTION - asserted, not
    %% assumed, by the def167 acceptance case that reads it back unfiltered), and no
    %% metric was added (the quarantine GAUGE still covers only the identity partition -
    %% recorded as deliberately-not-done, not as done).
    classDef def167changed fill:#e0f7fa,stroke:#00695c,stroke-width:2px;
    class valueShape,reservedIdentity,unparseableBody,pipeline,consumer,decisionRecord,decisionView,tableStoreQuery,hostInvocation def167changed;

    %% ── UC-ROC-117 — the Simulator publish WINDOW is stripped out entirely ──────────
    %% Owner instruction, 2026-09-08: "We can now remove everythign to do with the arming
    %% etc as we have proper oauth", then "plase strip that out of code docs runbooks etc".
    %%
    %% THE PREMISE, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED (deployed host, 2026-09-08): `/`,
    %% `/api/decisions`, `/api/simulator/capability` and `POST /api/simulator/publish` all
    %% answer 401 to an anonymous caller; `/health` and `/api/health` answer 200. Every part
    %% of the window mechanism traced back to ONE property - the write route was anonymously
    %% reachable and performs a real write that raises a real Jira ticket - and that property
    %% is gone. The access gate bounds WHO, where the window bounded WHEN, and it is the
    %% stronger of the two.
    %%
    %% REMOVED, as NODES: domain/simulatorPublishWindow (the four fail-closed rules, the
    %% 24h ceiling, the simpublish.window line, PUBLISH_WINDOW_ENV_VAR). The already-orphaned
    %% UC-ROC-107 subgraph went with it - see the note above the UC-ROC-105 block.
    %%
    %% BEHAVIOUR-CHANGED, each for a reason a tester should read:
    %%   simPublishApi     - gate 1 is GONE; six gates, and the `disabled` outcome cannot be
    %%                       emitted. The 200 body no longer carries `enabledUntil`. 403 is
    %%                       not a status this seam can answer.
    %%   simCapApi         - ONE state; no window fields; no 503; the budget is read on EVERY
    %%                       request rather than only while open.
    %%   simCapDisclosure  - state gating removed (capabilityKeysFor takes no argument) and
    %%                       the ledger's ANONYMITY PREMISE re-measured under A1.13.
    %%   simPublishForHost - resolves no window, emits NO composition line, and can no longer
    %%                       throw for a window reason. Its only remaining per-request clock
    %%                       use is the BUDGET KEY, which is why `now` still must not be frozen.
    %%   simCapForHost     - no window tier; delta 020 A1.6's "the closed path performs zero
    %%                       storage transactions" is RETIRED, not amended: there is no closed
    %%                       path, every read is one point lookup, and the caller is authenticated.
    %%   azureFunctionsHost- both route docstrings restated; the route SET is unchanged, so no
    %%                       registration pin moves.
    %%   readApi           - the local mirror answers the one state; no local env var opens
    %%                       anything.
    %%   simPublishBudget  - unchanged in code and PROMOTED in status: with the self-closing
    %%                       window gone, 50/15min + 2000/UTC-day is the only volume bound.
    %%                       Marked so a tester re-reads its refusal path, not because a line moved.
    %%   simulatorPage     - three resting strip states, not four; renamed vocabulary; the
    %%                       remaining-time span deleted; height parity RE-MEASURED in the
    %%                       real browser (58px x3, spread 0, at all four gate viewports).
    %%   publishCapabilityDomain - `closed` deleted, `unknown` untouched; `remainingText` and
    %%                       the `capability-disabled` branch deleted; the budget's period
    %%                       named and its refusal now scope-aware (AC-123-5, client-side).
    %%   publishApiClient  - the orphaned `postWindowChange` deleted; one of the mount-GET
    %%                       argument's three grounds retired with the `disabled` outcome.
    %%
    %% NOT MARKED, deliberately: the PORTS are untouched (no publisher, budget or store port
    %% signature changed); `allowedPublishTargets`/`reservedSimulatorNodes` are untouched (the
    %% destination guard and the reserved-node rule are exactly as they were, and are now
    %% carrying more of the safety case); `publishRateBucket` is untouched; and NO metric was
    %% added to replace the deleted `disabled` dimension - the replacement signal is the access
    %% gate's own 401s, which are App Service telemetry and not ours to emit. That last one is
    %% recorded as deliberately-not-done, not as done.
    classDef uc117changed fill:#fce4ec,stroke:#ad1457,stroke-width:2px;
    class simPublishApi,simCapApi,simCapDisclosure,simPublishForHost,simCapForHost,azureFunctionsHost,readApi,simPublishBudget,simulatorPage,publishCapabilityDomain,publishApiClient uc117changed;
